const MB2_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "היה קורא בתורה והגיע זמן המקרא אם כיון לבו יצא ואם לאו לא יצא.", "en": "If one were reading [the section of the Shema] in the Torah and the time for the recital [of the Shema] arrived — if he concentrated, he has fulfilled his obligation, and if not, he has not fulfilled his obligation.", "c": [["if he concentrated", "According to the view that mitzvoth require intent, \"If he concentrated\" is understood as: if he were intent upon fulfilling his obligation; and according to the view that mitzvoth do not require intent it is understood as: if he concentrated upon reciting it with the correct vocalization (as opposed to reciting it for proof-reading purposes, where he does not read the words as they are vocalized, but as they are written in order to discriminate between defective and plene forms, in which instance he does not fulfill his obligation). And we rule that mitzvoth require intent."]]}, {"he": "בפרקים שואל מפני הכבוד ומשיב.", "en": "Between sections he extends greeting out of honor, and he returns greeting.", "c": [["Between sections", "\"Between sections\" is explained later in our Mishnah."], ["greeting out of honor", "He extends greeting to one whose honor warrants it, such as his father, or his teacher, or one superior to him in wisdom"], ["and he returns greeting", "It goes without saying that he returns greeting to them if they greet him first."]]}, {"he": "ובאמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב דברי ר' מאיר.", "en": "And in the middle [of a section], he extends greeting out of fear, and he returns greeting. These are the words of R. Meir.", "c": [["greeting out of fear", "i.e., where he is afraid that the other might otherwise kill him. And it goes without saying that he returns greeting to him. But he may not do so out of honor"]]}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר באמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב מפני הכבוד בפרקים שואל מפני הכבוד ומשיב שלום לכל אדם:", "en": "R. Yehudah says: In the middle [of a section] he extends greeting out of fear, and returns greeting out of honor. Between sections he returns greeting to all men", "c": [["greeting out of honor", "i.e., in deference to one it is incumbent upon him to honor"], ["greeting to all men", "who greet him. And the halachah is in accordance with R. Yehudah. And wherever it is forbidden to interrupt the recital, it is forbidden to speak in the holy tongue as in any other language."]]}], [{"he": "אלו הן בין הפרקים בין ברכה ראשונה לשניה בין שניה לשמע ובין שמע לוהיה אם שמוע בין והיה אם שמוע לויאמר בין ויאמר לאמת ויציב.", "en": "The following constitutes \"between sections\": between the first blessing and the second, between the second and Shema, between Shema and vehaya im shamoa, between vehaya im shamoa and vayomer, between vayomer and emeth veyatziv.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר בין ויאמר לאמת ויציב לא יפסיק.", "en": "R. Yehudah says: It is forbidden to interrupt between vayomer and emeth veyatziv.", "c": [["vayomer and emeth veyatziv", "For it is written (Jeremiah 10:10): \"And the L-rd G-d is emeth.\" Therefore, it is forbidden to interrupt between ani hashem elokeichem and emeth. And this is the halachah."]]}, {"he": "אמר ר' יהושע בן קרחה למה קדמה שמע לוהיה אם שמוע אלא כדי שיקבל עליו עול מלכות שמים תחלה ואחר כך יקבל עליו עול מצות.", "en": "R. Yehoshua b. Karcha said: Why was Shema placed before vehaya im shamoa? So that one first take upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven, and thereafter the yoke of mitzvoth.", "c": []}, {"he": "והיה אם שמוע לויאמר שוהיה אם שמוע נוהג ביום ובלילה ויאמר אינו נוהג אלא ביום:", "en": "Why was vehaya im shamoa placed before vayomer? For vehaya im shamoa obtains both by day and by night, whereas vayomer obtains only by day.", "c": [["day and by night", "it being written therein (Deuteronomy 11:19): \"And you shall teach them to your sons\"; and the mitzvah of Torah study obtains both by day and by night."], ["obtains only by day", "For it contains the section of the mitzvah of tzitzith, which does not obtain at night, it being written (Numbers 15:39): \"And you shall see it.\""]]}], [{"he": "הקורא את שמע ולא השמיע לאזנו יצא.", "en": "One who recites the Shema without causing himself to hear it fulfills the obligation.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יוסי אומר לא יצא.", "en": "R. Yossi says: He does not fulfill the obligation.", "c": [["not fulfill the obligation", "For it is written (Deuteronomy 6:4): \"Hear\" — Let your ear hear what your mouth utters. And the first tanna holds: \"Hear\" — in any language that you are accustomed to hear. And the halachah is according to the first tanna."]]}, {"he": "קרא ולא דקדק באותיותיה רבי יוסי אומר יצא.", "en": "If he recited it without being precise with its letters — R. Yossi says: He has fulfilled his obligation.", "c": [["precise with its letters", "to enunciate them clearly, in an instance of two words where the second word begins with the same letter with which the first letter ends, as in \"al levavcha,\" \"esev besadecha,\" \"va'avadetem meherah.\" If he does not leave space between them to separate them, it sounds as if he is pronouncing two letters as one."], ["has fulfilled his obligation", "And the halachah is according to R. Yossi. However, ab initio, he must enunciate the letters. Likewise, he must take care not to rest the mobile sheva and not to move the quiescent, and not to weaken (by pronouncing without a dagesh) a strong form and not to strengthen a weak one. And he must accentuate the zayin of \"tizkeru,\" so that it does not sound like \"tiskeru,\" that is, \"so that you amass reward.\" For it is not fitting to serve the Master for the sake of reward."]]}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר לא יצא.", "en": "R. Yehudah says: He has not fulfilled his obligation.", "c": []}, {"he": "הקורא למפרע לא יצא.", "en": "If one recites it in inverted order, he has not fulfilled his obligation", "c": [["it in inverted order", "If he recites the third verse before the second, the second before the first, and the like"], ["not fulfilled his obligation", "it being written (Deuteronomy 6:6): \"and these words shall be\" — they shall remain in their original form, i.e., as they are ordered in the Torah. However, if he advances the section, reciting vayomer before vehaya im shamoa, and vehaya im shamoa before Shema, it would seem that this is not considered \"inverted,\" and he fulfills his obligation; for they are not thus arranged, one after the other, in the Torah."]]}, {"he": "קרא וטעה יחזור למקום שטעה:", "en": "If he recited it and erred, he returns to the point of the error.", "c": [["point of the error", "If he erred between one section and another, not knowing with which section he left off and to the beginning of which section he should return, he returns to the first verse, vehaya im shamoa. (Rambam says: Veahavta eth Hashem.) And if he stopped in the middle of a section, knowing which section, but not knowing where in that section he left off, he returns to the beginning of that section. If he recited \"uchethavtam,\" but did not know whether it were that of Shema or that of vehaya im shamoa, he returns to the \"uchethavtam\" of Shema. And if he were in doubt after he began leman yirbu, he does not return, for he can rely on \"the habit of his tongue.\""]]}], [{"he": "האומנין קורין בראש האילן או בראש הנדבך מה שאינן רשאין לעשות כן בתפלה:", "en": "Laborers may recite the Shema on the top of a tree or on top of a nidbach, something they are not permitted to do for tefillah (Shemoneh Esreh)", "c": [["top of a nidbach", "a stone ledge, as in (Ezra 6:4): \"nidbachin di even g'lal\" (\"rows of heavy stones\"). Though they are apprehensive of falling and cannot concentrate, the sages did not require them to descend; for only the first verse of the Shema requires concentration"], ["for tefillah (Shemoneh Esreh)", "for prayer is the imploration of mercy, and it requires concentration, so that they must descend to pray."]]}], [{"he": "חתן פטור מקריאת שמע בלילה הראשון עד מוצאי שבת אם לא עשה מעשה.", "en": "A bridegroom is exempt from the recital of the Shema the first night, until motzai Shabbath if he had not performed the act. After that time, he is \"familiar\" with her and no longer preoccupied, so that even if he had not yet performed the act, he must recite the Shema.]", "c": [["not performed the act", "A bridegroom who married a virgin is exempt from the recital of the Shema the first night, being preoccupied lest he not find her to be a virgin. And I have heard that (his preoccupation is) the fear that he might become kruth shafchah (mutilated) through intercourse, this being \"preoccupation of a mitzvah.\" And Scripture states (Deuteronomy 6:7): \"and in your walking upon the way\" — It is in your (mundane) \"walking\" that you are obliged to recite it, but not in that entailed by a mitzvah. \"if he had not performed the act\": if he had not had intercourse until motzai Shabbath, his \"preoccupation\" lasting four nights [from the customary day (Wednesday) of the wedding for a virgin"]]}, {"he": "מעשה ברבן גמליאל שקרא בלילה הראשון שנשא", "en": "It happened that R. Gamliel recited the Shema on his wedding night,", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שחתן פטור מקריאת שמע בלילה הראשון", "en": "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that a bridegroom is exempt from the Shema?\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר להם איני שומע לכם לבטל ממני מלכות שמים אפילו שעה אחת:", "en": "He answered: \"I will not heed you to divest myself of the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven for even a short while!\"", "c": []}], [{"he": "רחץ לילה הראשון שמתה אשתו", "en": "And he bathed the first night after the death of his wife,", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שאבל אסור לרחוץ", "en": "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that a mourner may not bathe?\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר להם איני כשאר כל אדם אסטניס אני:", "en": "He answered: \"I am not like most men; I am istanis.\"", "c": [["men; I am istanis.", "cold and prone to catch cold (from \"tzinah\" - \"cold\"). He would suffer if he did not bathe, and only bathing for pleasure is forbidden a mourner."]]}], [{"he": "וכשמת טבי עבדו קבל עליו תנחומין", "en": "And when Tevi, his bondsman, died, he accepted condolences for him,", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שאין מקבלין תנחומין על העבדים", "en": "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that it is forbidden to accept condolences for bondsmen?\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר להם אין טבי עבדי כשאר כל העבדים כשר היה:", "en": "He answered: \"Tevi, my bondsman, was not like other bondsmen; he was a man of integrity.\"", "c": []}], [{"he": "חתן אם רצה לקרות קריאת שמע לילה הראשון קורא", "en": "A bridegroom who desires to recite the Shema on his wedding night may do so.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבן שמעון בן גמליאל אומר לא כל הרוצה ליטול את השם יטול:", "en": "R. Shimon b. Gamliel said: \"Not all who wish to take the Name may do so.\"", "c": [["Name may do so.", "If he is not recognized as a sage and a porush (saintly) in other matters, this is nothing but pride, pluming oneself on exemplary powers of concentration. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Shimon b. Gamliel. We find some of our rabbis saying that today all men should recite the Shema on their wedding night. For since in these generations we do not recite it with much concentration on all the other days, if a bridegroom did not recite the Shema on his wedding night, he would seem even more haughty, giving the impression that he concentrated at all other times except this, being preoccupied with the mitzvah."]]}]];
const MB2_LESSONS=[{"id": "b2-1", "title": "Shema in the middle of learning", "short": "Perek 2 · Mishnah 1", "parts": [0], "phrases": [["היה קורא בתורה והגיע זמן המקרא אם כיון לבו יצא ואם לאו לא יצא", "If one were reading in the Torah and the time for the recital arrived — if he concentrated, he has fulfilled his obligation, and if not, he has not fulfilled his obligation."], ["בפרקים שואל מפני הכבוד ומשיב", "Between sections he extends greeting out of honor, and he returns greeting."], ["ובאמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב דברי ר' מאיר", "And in the middle, he extends greeting out of fear, and he returns greeting. These are the words of R. Meir."], ["ר' יהודה אומר באמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב מפני הכבוד בפרקים שואל מפני הכבוד ומשיב שלום לכל אדם", "R. Yehudah says: In the middle he extends greeting out of fear, and returns greeting out of honor. Between sections he returns greeting to all men"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“if he concentrated” — According to the view that mitzvoth require intent, \"If he concentrated\" is understood as: if he were intent upon fulfilling his obligation;"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one were reading in the Torah and the time for the recital arrived — if he…", "tiles": ["היה קורא", "בתורה והגיע", "זמן", "המקרא"], "decoys": ["דברי"], "id": "b2-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What decides whether he fulfilled the mitzvah of Shema?", "opts": ["Whether he had kavanah", "Whether he read aloud", "Whether he was standing", "Whether he was in shul"], "a": 0, "ex": "אם כיון לבו יצא, ואם לאו לא יצא.", "id": "b2-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“greeting out of fear” — i.e., where he is afraid that the other might otherwise kill him. And it goes without saying that he returns greeting to him. But he may not do so out of honor"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "tf", "q": "According to R' Yehudah, between sections one may return a greeting to anyone.", "a": true, "ex": "בפרקים... ומשיב שלום לכל אדם.", "id": "b2-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ובאמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב דברי ר'", "after": "", "opts": ["מאיר", "מהרהר", "אומר"], "a": 0, "ex": "ובאמצע שואל מפני היראה ומשיב דברי ר' מאיר", "id": "b2-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b2-2", "title": "Why Shema comes first", "short": "Perek 2 · Mishnah 2", "parts": [1], "phrases": [["אלו הן בין הפרקים בין ברכה ראשונה לשניה בין שניה לשמע ובין שמע לוהיה אם שמוע בין והיה אם שמוע לויאמר בין ויאמר לאמת ויציב", "The following constitutes \"between sections\": between the first blessing and the second, between the second and Shema, between Shema and vehaya im shamoa, between vehaya im shamoa and vayomer, between vayomer and emeth veyatziv."], ["רבי יהודה אומר בין ויאמר לאמת ויציב לא יפסיק", "R. Yehudah says: It is forbidden to interrupt between vayomer and emeth veyatziv."], ["אמר ר' יהושע בן קרחה למה קדמה שמע לוהיה אם שמוע אלא כדי שיקבל עליו עול מלכות שמים תחלה ואחר כך יקבל עליו עול מצות", "R. Yehoshua b. Karcha said: Why was Shema placed before vehaya im shamoa? So that one first take upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven, and thereafter the yoke of mitzvoth."], ["והיה אם שמוע לויאמר שוהיה אם שמוע נוהג ביום ובלילה ויאמר אינו נוהג אלא ביום", "Why was vehaya im shamoa placed before vayomer? For vehaya im shamoa obtains both by day and by night, whereas vayomer obtains only by day."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“vayomer and emeth veyatziv” — For it is written (Jeremiah 10:10): \"And the L-rd G-d is emeth.\" Therefore, it is forbidden to interrupt between ani hashem elokeichem and emeth. And this is the halachah."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "The following constitutes \"between sections\": between the first blessing and the second,…", "tiles": ["אלו הן", "בין הפרקים", "בין", "ברכה"], "decoys": ["ביום"], "id": "b2-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Why does שמע come before והיה אם שמוע?", "opts": ["To accept the yoke of Heaven first, then the yoke of mitzvos", "Because it is shorter", "Because it was written first", "Because it is said standing"], "a": 0, "ex": "כדי שיקבל עליו עול מלכות שמים תחלה.", "id": "b2-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“day and by night” — it being written therein (Deuteronomy 11:19): \"And you shall teach them to your sons\"; and the mitzvah of Torah study obtains both by day and by night."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Why does והיה אם שמוע come before ויאמר?", "opts": ["והיה אם שמוע applies day and night; ויאמר only by day", "ויאמר is longer", "ויאמר is from Bamidbar", "No reason is given"], "a": 0, "ex": "שוהיה אם שמוע נוהג ביום ובלילה, ויאמר אינו נוהג אלא ביום.", "id": "b2-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "אמר ר' יהושע בן קרחה למה קדמה שמע לוהיה אם שמוע אלא כדי שיקבל עליו עול מלכות שמים תחלה ואחר כך יקבל עליו עול", "after": "", "opts": ["מצות", "שאין", "מבית"], "a": 0, "ex": "אמר ר' יהושע בן קרחה למה קדמה שמע לוהיה אם שמוע אלא כדי שיקבל עליו עול מלכות שמים תחלה ואחר כך יקבל עליו עול מצות", "id": "b2-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b2-3", "title": "Saying Shema properly", "short": "Perek 2 · Mishnah 3–4", "parts": [2, 3], "phrases": [["הקורא את שמע ולא השמיע לאזנו יצא", "One who recites the Shema without causing himself to hear it fulfills the obligation."], ["רבי יוסי אומר לא יצא", "R. Yossi says: He does not fulfill the obligation."], ["קרא ולא דקדק באותיותיה רבי יוסי אומר יצא", "If he recited it without being precise with its letters — R. Yossi says: He has fulfilled his obligation."], ["ר' יהודה אומר לא יצא", "R. Yehudah says: He has not fulfilled his obligation."], ["הקורא למפרע לא יצא", "If one recites it in inverted order, he has not fulfilled his obligation"], ["קרא וטעה יחזור למקום שטעה", "If he recited it and erred, he returns to the point of the error."], ["האומנין קורין בראש האילן או בראש הנדבך מה שאינן רשאין לעשות כן בתפלה", "Laborers may recite the Shema on the top of a tree or on top of a nidbach, something they are not permitted to do for tefillah (Shemoneh Esreh)"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 6, "note": ["Bartenura", "“not fulfill the obligation” — For it is written (Deuteronomy 6:4): \"Hear\" — Let your ear hear what your mouth utters. And the first tanna holds: \"Hear\" — in any language that you are accustomed to hear. And the halachah is according to the first tanna."], "mref": 2}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "One who recites the Shema without causing himself to hear it fulfills the obligation.", "tiles": ["הקורא את", "שמע ולא", "השמיע", "לאזנו"], "decoys": ["יחזור"], "id": "b2-3-1"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "According to the first opinion, one who says Shema without hearing his own voice has fulfilled the mitzvah.", "a": true, "ex": "הקורא את שמע ולא השמיע לאזנו יצא.", "id": "b2-3-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What if one says Shema out of order (למפרע)?", "opts": ["He has not fulfilled it", "He has fulfilled it", "He repeats only the last pasuk", "It depends on the time of day"], "a": 0, "ex": "הקורא למפרע לא יצא.", "id": "b2-3-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 6, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“top of a nidbach” — a stone ledge, as in (Ezra 6:4): \"nidbachin di even g'lal\" (\"rows of heavy stones\"). Though they are apprehensive of falling and cannot concentrate, the sages did not require them to descend;"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where may laborers say Shema?", "opts": ["At the top of a tree or a wall", "Only on the ground", "Only in shul", "Only after work"], "a": 0, "ex": "קורין בראש האילן או בראש הנדבך.", "id": "b2-3-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ר' יהודה אומר לא", "after": "", "opts": ["יצא", "אותו", "גמליאל"], "a": 0, "ex": "ר' יהודה אומר לא יצא", "id": "b2-3-5"}]}, {"id": "b2-4", "title": "Rabban Gamliel's ways", "short": "Perek 2 · Mishnah 5–8", "parts": [4, 5, 6, 7], "phrases": [["חתן פטור מקריאת שמע בלילה הראשון עד מוצאי שבת אם לא עשה מעשה", "A bridegroom is exempt from the recital of the Shema the first night, until motzai Shabbath if he had not performed the act. After that time, he is \"familiar\" with her and no longer preoccupied, so that even if he had not yet performed the act, he must recite the Shema.]"], ["מעשה ברבן גמליאל שקרא בלילה הראשון שנשא", "It happened that R. Gamliel recited the Shema on his wedding night,"], ["אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שחתן פטור מקריאת שמע בלילה הראשון", "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that a bridegroom is exempt from the Shema?\""], ["אמר להם איני שומע לכם לבטל ממני מלכות שמים אפילו שעה אחת", "He answered: \"I will not heed you to divest myself of the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven for even a short while!\""], ["רחץ לילה הראשון שמתה אשתו", "And he bathed the first night after the death of his wife,"], ["אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שאבל אסור לרחוץ", "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that a mourner may not bathe?\""], ["אמר להם איני כשאר כל אדם אסטניס אני", "He answered: \"I am not like most men; I am istanis.\""], ["וכשמת טבי עבדו קבל עליו תנחומין", "And when Tevi, his bondsman, died, he accepted condolences for him,"], ["אמרו לו תלמידיו לא למדתנו רבינו שאין מקבלין תנחומין על העבדים", "at which his disciples said to him: \"Did our master not teach us that it is forbidden to accept condolences for bondsmen?\""], ["אמר להם אין טבי עבדי כשאר כל העבדים כשר היה", "He answered: \"Tevi, my bondsman, was not like other bondsmen; he was a man of integrity.\""], ["חתן אם רצה לקרות קריאת שמע לילה הראשון קורא", "A bridegroom who desires to recite the Shema on his wedding night may do so."], ["רבן שמעון בן גמליאל אומר לא כל הרוצה ליטול את השם יטול", "R. Shimon b. Gamliel said: \"Not all who wish to take the Name may do so.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“not performed the act” — A bridegroom who married a virgin is exempt from the recital of the Shema the first night, being preoccupied lest he not find her to be a virgin."], "mref": 4}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "A bridegroom is exempt from the recital of the Shema the first night, until motzai…", "tiles": ["חתן פטור", "מקריאת שמע", "בלילה", "הראשון"], "decoys": ["יטול"], "id": "b2-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Why did Rabban Gamliel say Shema on his wedding night?", "opts": ["He would not remove the yoke of Heaven even for a moment", "He forgot the halacha", "His talmidim asked him to", "It was Shabbos"], "a": 0, "ex": "איני שומע לכם לבטל ממני מלכות שמים אפילו שעה אחת.", "id": "b2-4-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“men; I am istanis.” — cold and prone to catch cold (from \"tzinah\" - \"cold\"). He would suffer if he did not bathe, and only bathing for pleasure is forbidden a mourner."], "mref": 5}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How did Rabban Gamliel describe Tevi?", "opts": ["כשר היה — he was a worthy man", "He was a talmid chacham", "He was a kohen", "He was his relative"], "a": 0, "ex": "אין טבי עבדי כשאר כל העבדים, כשר היה.", "id": "b2-4-3"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel holds that not everyone who wishes to 'take the Name' may do so.", "a": true, "ex": "לא כל הרוצה ליטול את השם יטול.", "id": "b2-4-4"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 7, "to": 10, "note": null, "mref": 6}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "אמר להם איני כשאר כל אדם אסטניס", "after": "", "opts": ["אני", "ואת", "חדש"], "a": 0, "ex": "אמר להם איני כשאר כל אדם אסטניס אני", "id": "b2-4-5"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 10, "to": 12, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Name may do so.” — If he is not recognized as a sage and a porush (saintly) in other matters, this is nothing but pride, pluming oneself on exemplary powers of concentration. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Shimon b. Gamliel."], "mref": 7}]}];
const MB3_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "מי שמתו מוטל לפניו פטור מקריאת שמע מן התפלה ומן התפילין", "en": "One whose dead one is lying before him, is exempt from the recital of the Shema [being preoccupied with a mitzvah], from tefillah, and from tefillin.", "c": [["One whose dead one", "(one of his kin that he is obliged to mourn, whom it is incumbent upon him to bury)"]]}, {"he": "נושאי המטה וחלופיהן וחלופי חלופיהן את שלפני המטה ואת שלאחר המטה", "en": "As to the litter bearers, their replacements, and the latter's replacements, those before the litter, and those behind it —", "c": [["litter bearers, their replacements", "it being the practice to alternate, all wishing to partake in the mitzvah"], ["those before the litter", "those set to carry it when it reaches them"], ["and those behind it", "that is, both those before it and those behind it"]]}, {"he": "את שלמטה צורך בהן פטורין", "en": "those whose services are required [for carrying the litter], are exempt;", "c": []}, {"he": "ואת שאין למטה צורך בהן חייבין.", "en": "and those whose services are not required are obligated.", "c": [["services are not required", "such as those who go only to accompany the deceased to honor him"]]}, {"he": "אלו ואלו פטורים מן התפלה:", "en": "And both are exempt from tefillah,", "c": [["are exempt from tefillah", "it not being Scripturally mandated as is the recital of the Shema. And some say because it requires a greater measure of concentration."]]}], [{"he": "קברו את המת וחזרו", "en": "Once they bury the dead and return —", "c": []}, {"he": "אם יכולין להתחיל ולגמור עד שלא יגיעו לשורה יתחילו", "en": "if they can begin and finish [one section of the Shema] before they arrive at the file, they should begin;", "c": [["arrive at the file", "They would make files of mourners to comfort him upon returning from the grave."]]}, {"he": "ואם לאו לא יתחילו", "en": "and if not, they should not begin.", "c": [["and if not", "If the distance from the grave to the place where they made the file was short, so that there was no time to being and finish before arriving at the file"]]}, {"he": "העומדים בשורה הפנימים פטורים והחיצונים חייבין:", "en": "Those who stand in the file — the inner ones [(who see the mourners)] are exempt; the outer ones are obligated.", "c": []}], [{"he": "נשים ועבדים וקטנים פטורין מקריאת שמע ומן התפילין וחייבין בתפלה ובמזוזה ובברכת המזון:", "en": "Women, bondsmen, and minors are exempt from the Shema and from tefillin. And tefillah, mezuzah, and the recital of grace are binding upon them.", "c": [["Shema and from tefillin", "Even though the Shema is a time-oriented positive commandment (mitzvath aseh shehazman grama), a class of mitzvah from which women are exempt, we would think that it is, nonetheless, binding upon them because it contains the acceptance of the kingdom of Heaven — for which reason we must be apprised otherwise. And the mitzvah of tefillin is a time-oriented positive commandment, for it does not obtain at night and on the Sabbath; but we would think that since it is likened to mezuzah, it is binding upon women. We must, therefore, be apprised otherwise. \"Minors\": A father is not obligated to train in the recital of the Shema even a minor who had arrived at the age of training; for the son is not always to be found with his father at the time of recital. And a father was not obligated to train a minor in the mitzvah of tefillin, for he cannot be expected to guard himself against expelling air while wearing them."], ["are binding upon them", "For tefillah is the imploration of mercy, and a rabbinical ordinance; and it was instituted for women, too, and for the training of minors. \"Mezuzah\": We might think, since mezuzah is likened to Torah study, that just as women are exempt from Torah study, it being written (Deuteronomy 11:9): \"And you shall teach them to your sons\" — and not to your daughters, they should, likewise, be exempt from mezuzah, even though it is not a time-oriented positive commandment; we are, therefore, apprised otherwise. \"The recital of grace\": It is open to question whether the recital of grace is Scripturally binding upon women, it being written (Deuteronomy 8:10): \"And you shall eat, and you shall be sated, and you shall bless\" — so that it is a non time-oriented positive commandment — or whether it is not Scripturally binding upon women, it being written (Ibid.): \"for the good land which He has given you\"; and the land was not given to females. The question was not resolved."]]}], [{"he": "בעל קרי מהרהר בלבו ואינו מברך לא לפניה ולא לאחריה.", "en": "One who had a seminal discharge meditates, and he does not make the blessing before or after it", "c": [["had a seminal discharge", "(Ezra instituted that one who had experienced a seminal discharge, whether inadvertently or wittingly, should not read in the Torah until he had immersed himself — not because of cleanliness or uncleanliness, for words of Torah are not susceptible of uncleanliness — but so that Torah scholars not be always \"found with their wives like roosters.\")"], ["a seminal discharge meditates", "upon the Shema in his heart [when the time for its recital arrives"], ["before or after it", "even by way of meditation. Since the blessings are not Scripturally mandated, the rabbis did not require them."]]}, {"he": "ועל המזון מברך לאחריו ואינו מברך לפניו.", "en": "And for bread, he makes the concluding blessing [this being Scripturally mandated], but not the preliminary one", "c": [["not the preliminary one", "this not being Scripturally mandated. And it has already been ruled, with none demurring, that the immersion requirement has been rescinded and that those who had experienced a seminal discharge recite the Shema in the usual manner and study Torah and pray, and recite all of the blessings."]]}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר מברך לפניהם ולאחריהם:", "en": "R. Yehudah says: He makes both the preliminary and the concluding blessing.", "c": []}], [{"he": "היה עומד בתפלה ונזכר שהוא בעל קרי לא יפסיק אלא יקצר.", "en": "If in the middle of tefillah (shemoneh esreh) he remembered that he had experienced a seminal discharge, he should not break off [his prayer entirely], but he should shorten [each blessing].", "c": []}, {"he": "ירד לטבול אם יכול לעלות ולהתכסות ולקרות עד שלא תנץ החמה יעלה ויתכסה ויקרא", "en": "If he had gone down to immerse himself — if he can come up, cover himself, and recite the Shema before sunrise, he should do so.", "c": [["he should do so", "For the vatikin (the exceptionally pious) are exacting with themselves to conclude it at sunrise, it being written (Psalms 72:5): \"They shall fear You with the sun.\""]]}, {"he": "ואם לאו יתכסה במים ויקרא.", "en": "And if not, he should cover himself with the water and recite it.", "c": [["water and recite it", "And only in clouded water, where his nakedness is not exposed, but not in clear water."]]}, {"he": "אבל לא יתכסה לא במים הרעים ולא במי המשרה עד שיטיל לתוכן מים.", "en": "But he should not cover himself with bad [i.e., foul] water, or with steeping water [water in which flax is steeped], until he dilutes it.", "c": [["until he dilutes it", "There is something missing here. It is to be understood thus: \"And he should not recite it near urine until he has diluted it.\" The amount of water for diluting a single urinal discharge is a revi'ith."]]}, {"he": "וכמה ירחיק מהם ומן הצואה ארבע אמות:", "en": "And how far should one remove himself from it [from undiluted urine] and from feces\" Four ells.", "c": [["from feces\" Four ells", "And only when it is to the side of him or behind him; but if it is in front of him, he must remove himself until it is out of sight."]]}], [{"he": "זב שראה קרי. ונדה שפלטה שכבת זרע. והמשמשת שראתה נדה. צריכין טבילה. ורבי יהודה פוטר:", "en": "A zav (one suffering from a genital flow) who discharged semen, a niddah who emitted semen, and a woman who had intercourse and became a niddah must undergo ritual immersion. And R. Yehudah does not require it.", "c": [["must undergo ritual immersion", "A zav who discharged semen: Though he is unclean seven days because of zav uncleanliness, and this immersion does not render him clean, still, he must undergo this immersion for words of Torah because of the semen discharge, as instituted by Ezra. Likewise, a niddah who wishes to pray and emits semen (from a prior intercourse) is regarded as one discharging semen. And such an emission of semen renders a woman unclean for three days after intercourse. After that time it putrefies in her body and is no longer viable. And it is to be understood thus: \"A niddah who emitted, now, semen from an intercourse prior to her becoming a niddah, and a woman who had intercourse — one who, after intercourse, became a niddah — must undergo ritual immersion."], ["does not require it", "R. Yehudah does not require it even in the instance of a woman who after intercourse became a niddah, even though ab initio she must undergo ritual immersion and it can be contended that the immersion obligation does not leave her. And we have already written above that this immersion ordinance was rescinded, being \"an ordinance by which the majority of the congregation cannot abide.\""]]}]];
const MB3_LESSONS=[{"id": "b3-1", "title": "Busy with a mitzvah", "short": "Perek 3 · Mishnah 1", "parts": [0], "phrases": [["מי שמתו מוטל לפניו פטור מקריאת שמע מן התפלה ומן התפילין", "One whose dead one is lying before him, is exempt from the recital of the Shema, from tefillah, and from tefillin."], ["נושאי המטה וחלופיהן וחלופי חלופיהן את שלפני המטה ואת שלאחר המטה", "As to the litter bearers, their replacements, and the latter's replacements, those before the litter, and those behind it —"], ["את שלמטה צורך בהן פטורין", "those whose services are required, are exempt;"], ["ואת שאין למטה צורך בהן חייבין", "and those whose services are not required are obligated."], ["אלו ואלו פטורים מן התפלה", "And both are exempt from tefillah,"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“One whose dead one” — (one of his kin that he is obliged to mourn, whom it is incumbent upon him to bury)"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "One whose dead one is lying before him, is exempt from the recital of the Shema, from…", "tiles": ["מי שמתו", "מוטל לפניו", "פטור", "מקריאת"], "decoys": ["התפלה"], "id": "b3-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Who is exempt from Shema, tefillah and tefillin?", "opts": ["One whose deceased relative lies before him, before burial", "Anyone at a wedding", "Travelers", "Anyone in the year of mourning"], "a": 0, "ex": "מי שמתו מוטל לפניו.", "id": "b3-1-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Bearers whose help isn't needed for carrying are obligated in Shema.", "a": true, "ex": "ואת שאין למטה צורך בהן חייבין.", "id": "b3-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "את שלמטה צורך בהן", "after": "", "opts": ["פטורין", "אלא", "מכזית"], "a": 0, "ex": "את שלמטה צורך בהן פטורין", "id": "b3-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b3-2", "title": "After the levayah; who is obligated", "short": "Perek 3 · Mishnah 2–3", "parts": [1, 2], "phrases": [["קברו את המת וחזרו", "Once they bury the dead and return —"], ["אם יכולין להתחיל ולגמור עד שלא יגיעו לשורה יתחילו", "if they can begin and finish before they arrive at the file, they should begin;"], ["ואם לאו לא יתחילו", "and if not, they should not begin."], ["העומדים בשורה הפנימים פטורים והחיצונים חייבין", "Those who stand in the file — the inner ones are exempt; the outer ones are obligated."], ["נשים ועבדים וקטנים פטורין מקריאת שמע ומן התפילין וחייבין בתפלה ובמזוזה ובברכת המזון", "Women, bondsmen, and minors are exempt from the Shema and from tefillin. And tefillah, mezuzah, and the recital of grace are binding upon them."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“arrive at the file” — They would make files of mourners to comfort him upon returning from the grave."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "Once they bury the dead and return —", "tiles": ["קברו", "את", "המת", "וחזרו"], "decoys": ["ואם"], "id": "b3-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "In the line of comforters (שורה), who is exempt?", "opts": ["The inner row, who face the mourners", "The outer row", "Everyone", "No one"], "a": 0, "ex": "הפנימים פטורים והחיצונים חייבין.", "id": "b3-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Shema and from tefillin” — Even though the Shema is a time-oriented positive commandment (mitzvath aseh shehazman grama), a class of mitzvah from which women are exempt, we would think that it is, nonetheless, binding upon them because it contains the acceptance of…"], "mref": 2}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Women, bondsmen and minors are obligated in which of these?", "opts": ["Mezuzah", "Tefillin", "Kriyas Shema", "None of them"], "a": 0, "ex": "וחייבין בתפלה ובמזוזה ובברכת המזון.", "id": "b3-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ואם לאו לא", "after": "", "opts": ["יתחילו", "מזמנין", "הערב"], "a": 0, "ex": "ואם לאו לא יתחילו", "id": "b3-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b3-3", "title": "Purity before berachos", "short": "Perek 3 · Mishnah 4–6", "parts": [3, 4, 5], "phrases": [["בעל קרי מהרהר בלבו ואינו מברך לא לפניה ולא לאחריה", "One who had a seminal discharge meditates, and he does not make the blessing before or after it"], ["ועל המזון מברך לאחריו ואינו מברך לפניו", "And for bread, he makes the concluding blessing, but not the preliminary one"], ["ר' יהודה אומר מברך לפניהם ולאחריהם", "R. Yehudah says: He makes both the preliminary and the concluding blessing."], ["היה עומד בתפלה ונזכר שהוא בעל קרי לא יפסיק אלא יקצר", "If in the middle of tefillah (shemoneh esreh) he remembered that he had experienced a seminal discharge, he should not break off, but he should shorten."], ["ירד לטבול אם יכול לעלות ולהתכסות ולקרות עד שלא תנץ החמה יעלה ויתכסה ויקרא", "If he had gone down to immerse himself — if he can come up, cover himself, and recite the Shema before sunrise, he should do so."], ["ואם לאו יתכסה במים ויקרא", "And if not, he should cover himself with the water and recite it."], ["אבל לא יתכסה לא במים הרעים ולא במי המשרה עד שיטיל לתוכן מים", "But he should not cover himself with bad water, or with steeping water, until he dilutes it."], ["וכמה ירחיק מהם ומן הצואה ארבע אמות", "And how far should one remove himself from it and from feces\" Four ells."], ["זב שראה קרי. ונדה שפלטה שכבת זרע. והמשמשת שראתה נדה. צריכין טבילה. ורבי יהודה פוטר", "A zav (one suffering from a genital flow) who discharged semen, a niddah who emitted semen, and a woman who had intercourse and became a niddah must undergo ritual immersion. And R. Yehudah does not require it."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“had a seminal discharge” — (Ezra instituted that one who had experienced a seminal discharge, whether inadvertently or wittingly, should not read in the Torah until he had immersed himself — not because of cleanliness or uncleanliness, for words of Torah are not…"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "One who had a seminal discharge meditates, and he does not make the blessing before or…", "tiles": ["בעל קרי", "מהרהר בלבו", "ואינו", "מברך"], "decoys": ["ולקרות"], "id": "b3-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "In 3:4, what does R' Yehudah say about the berachos?", "opts": ["They are said before and after", "Only after", "Only before", "Not at all"], "a": 0, "ex": "מברך לפניהם ולאחריהם.", "id": "b3-3-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 4, "note": null, "mref": 4}, {"t": "tf", "q": "If one remembers in middle of Shemoneh Esrei, the mishnah says not to stop, but to shorten.", "a": true, "ex": "לא יפסיק אלא יקצר.", "id": "b3-3-3"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How far must one distance himself before saying Shema?", "opts": ["Four amos", "Two amos", "Ten amos", "Out of sight only"], "a": 0, "ex": "וכמה ירחיק מהם ומן הצואה ארבע אמות.", "id": "b3-3-4"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 8, "note": ["Bartenura", "“he should do so” — For the vatikin (the exceptionally pious) are exacting with themselves to conclude it at sunrise, it being written (Psalms 72:5): \"They shall fear You with the sun.\""], "mref": 4}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ירד לטבול אם יכול לעלות ולהתכסות ולקרות עד שלא תנץ החמה יעלה ויתכסה", "after": "", "opts": ["ויקרא", "שמוע", "ידי"], "a": 0, "ex": "ירד לטבול אם יכול לעלות ולהתכסות ולקרות עד שלא תנץ החמה יעלה ויתכסה ויקרא", "id": "b3-3-5"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 8, "to": 9, "note": ["Bartenura", "“must undergo ritual immersion” — A zav who discharged semen: Though he is unclean seven days because of zav uncleanliness, and this immersion does not render him clean, still, he must undergo this immersion for words of Torah because of the semen discharge, as instituted…"], "mref": 5}]}];
const MB4_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "תפלת השחר עד חצות.", "en": "The morning prayer may be recited until midday.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר עד ארבע שעות", "en": "R. Yehudah says: Until the fourth hour.", "c": [["Until the fourth hour", "For, according to the Rabbis, the daily burnt-offering may be sacrificed until midday; and, according to R. Yehudah, until the fourth hour of the day. \"Until the fourth hour\" is until the end of the fourth hour, a third of the day when the day is twelve hours long. And its time is always until the end of a third of the day according to the relative length or shortness of the day, as stated above in respect to the Shema. And the halachah is according to R. Yehudah."]]}, {"he": "תפלת המנחה עד הערב.", "en": "The afternoon prayer may be recited until the evening [i.e., until it gets dark.]", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר עד פלג המנחה.", "en": "R. Yehudah says: Until midway through the day (plag haminchah).", "c": [["the day (plag haminchah)", "The time of minchah ketanah (\"the small minchah\") is from nine and a half hours until nightfall — two and a half hours — so that plag haminchah, which is half of that, is an hour and a quarter (before nightfall). The ruling in this regard is that one may follow either practice. If he wishes to follow the sages and to recite the afternoon prayer until the evening, he may do so, so long as he does not recite the evening prayer at that time. For since he considers it day as far as the minchah prayer is concerned, he cannot consider it evening for purposes of the evening prayer. And if he wishes to follow R. Yehudah, to recite the afternoon prayer only until the plag haminchah, an hour and a quarter before nightfall, he may do so; and from that time on, he may recite the evening prayer."]]}, {"he": "תפלת הערב אין לה קבע", "en": "The evening prayer has no fixed time.", "c": [["has no fixed time", "Its time is the entire night. It is taught: \"it has no fixed time,\" rather than: \"its time is the entire night,\" for the evening prayer is optional, corresponding, as it does, to the time of the consumption of the limbs and fat-pieces — the entire night. And the latter is optional; for once the blood has been sprinkled, the offering is accepted, even if the limbs and fat-pieces become unclean or are lost. Today, however, it (the evening prayer) has been accepted as binding."]]}, {"he": "ושל מוספין כל היום", "en": "And the mussaf (\"additional\") prayer may be recited the entire day.", "c": [["recited the entire day", "If he delayed reciting it until after the seventh hour he fulfills the obligation, but he is called \"an offender.\" And this is the halachah."]]}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר עד שבע שעות:", "en": "R. Yehudah says: Until the seventh hour.", "c": []}], [{"he": "רבי נחוניה בן הקנה היה מתפלל בכניסתו לבית המדרש וביציאתו תפלה קצרה", "en": "R. Nechuniah b. Hakannah would recite a short prayer upon entering the house of study and upon leaving it.", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו לו מה מקום לתפלה זו.", "en": "When asked: \"What is the place [i.e., the nature] of this prayer?\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר להם בכניסתי אני מתפלל שלא תארע תקלה על ידי", "en": "he replied: \"Upon entering I pray that no mischance occur because of me\"; \"", "c": [["occur because of me", "that I not create a stumbling-block, as explained in the baraitha: \"that I not err in a halachah and my friends rejoice (in my discomfiture)\" — whereby I become the cause of evil, my friends being punished because of me"]]}, {"he": "וביציאתי אני נותן הודיה על חלקי:", "en": "and upon leaving, I give thanks for my portion.\"", "c": [["thanks for my portion.", "I thank Him for the good that He bestowed upon me in placing my portion among those who sit in the house of study. These two prayers, upon entering the house of study and upon leaving it, are binding upon all men. For thus is it stated in the baraitha: \"Upon entering what does he say?\" and \"Upon leaving what does he say?\", the implication being that he must say them."]]}], [{"he": "רבן גמליאל אומר בכל יום מתפלל אדם שמונה עשרה.", "en": "R. Gamliel says: One recites eighteen blessings (shemoneh esreh) every day.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יהושע אומר מעין שמונה עשרה.", "en": "R. Yehoshua says: What is akin to eighteen blessings.", "c": [["akin to eighteen blessings", "In the gemara, some explain that he recites each of the middle blessings in short and concludes with the blessing for each one; and others, that he says: \"Cause us, O L-rd our G-d, to know Your ways\" (havineinu), which is one blessing epitomizing all of the middle blessings of the shemoneh esreh, and he concludes: \"Blessed are you, O L-rd, who listens to prayer.\""]]}, {"he": "ר' עקיבא אומר אם שגורה תפלתו בפיו יתפלל שמונה עשרה ואם לאו מעין שמונה עשרה:", "en": "R. Akiva says: If it (the shemoneh esreh) is \"habitual\" in his mouth, [if he is \"taught\" and fluent in it], he recites shemoneh esreh; if not, he recites what is akin to it.", "c": [["is akin to it", "And the halachah is according to R. Akiva, that if one is not fluent in it, or is hard-pressed, he recites the first three blessings and the last, and \"Havineinu,\" in the middle, Havineinu epitomizing all of the middle blessings (with the exception of the rainy season, when he does not recite Havineinu, it being necessary for him to recite the request for rain in the blessing of the years; and with the exception of the conclusion of Sabbaths and festivals, when he must recite havdalah in chonen hada'ath."]]}], [{"he": "רבי אליעזר אומר העושה תפלתו קבע אין תפלתו תחנונים", "en": "R. Eliezer says: If one makes his prayer k'va, it is not accounted supplication.", "c": [["makes his prayer k'va", "so that his prayer feels burdensome to him. \"k'va\" — \"It is chok kavua (\"a fixed statute\") for me to pray, and I must 'deliver myself' of it.\""]]}, {"he": "רבי יהושע אומר המהלך במקום סכנה מתפלל תפלה קצרה", "en": "R. Yehoshua says: One who walks in a place of danger recites a short prayer. [And what is the short prayer?]", "c": []}, {"he": "אומר הושע השם את עמך את שארית ישראל בכל פרשת העבור יהיו צרכיהם לפניך ברוך אתה ה' שומע תפלה:", "en": "He says: \"Help, O L-rd, Your people, the remnant of Israel; bechal parashath haibur, let their needs be before You. Blessed are You, O L-rd, who listens to prayer.\"", "c": [["Israel; bechal parashath haibur", "\"even when they go astray (porshim) into transgression\""], ["who listens to prayer.", "Let their needs be revealed before You to have mercy upon them. \"parashath\" — as in \"perishah\" (separation). \"haibur\" — of aveirah (transgression). And the halachah is not in accordance with R. Yehoshua, but the prayer one recites in a place of danger is: \"The needs of Your people are many, etc.\" One recites it while walking, and he recites neither the first three nor the last three blessings (of the shemoneh esreh). And when he leaves the place of danger and his mind is at rest, he must recite the tefillah as usual if its time has not passed."]]}], [{"he": "היה רוכב על החמור ירד.", "en": "If he were riding on an ass, he dismounts (to pray).", "c": [["he dismounts (to pray)", "The halachah is not in accordance with this anonymous Mishnah; but whether or not he had someone to hold his ass, he does not dismount, for his mind is not settled (enough for prayer) if he must dismount."]]}, {"he": "ואם אינו יכול לירד יחזיר את פניו.", "en": "And if he cannot dismount, he turns his face", "c": [["he turns his face", "towards Jerusalem, it being written (I Kings 8:48): \"And they shall pray to You towards their land.\""]]}, {"he": "ואם אינו יכול להחזיר את פניו יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים:", "en": "And if he cannot turn his face, he directs his thoughts to the holy of holies", "c": [["the holy of holies", "it being written (Chronicles 6:26): \"And they will pray to this place.\""]]}], [{"he": "היה יושב בספינה או בקרון או באסדא יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים:", "en": "If he were sitting in a boat, in a wagon, or on an asda, he directs his thoughts to the holy of holies.", "c": [["or on an asda", "many pieces of wood tied and fastened together, used for sailing on a river. (In Scripture, (II Chronicles 2:15) these are called \"rafsodoth\")"]]}], [{"he": "רבי אלעזר בן עזריה אומר אין תפלת המוספין אלא בחבר עיר", "en": "R. Elazar b. Azaryah says: The mussaf (\"additional\") prayer is recited only bechever ir", "c": [["recited only bechever ir", "bechavurath ha'ir (\"with a company of the city\"); that is, with a congregation, and not individually."]]}, {"he": "וחכמים אומרים בחבר עיר ושלא בחבר עיר", "en": "And the sages say: Bechever ir and not bechever ir", "c": [["and not bechever ir", "both with a congregation and individually."]]}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר משמו כל מקום שיש חבר עיר היחיד פטור מתפלת המוספין:", "en": "R. Yehudah says in his [R. Elazar's] name: Wherever there is a congregation, an individual is exempt from the recitation of the mussaf prayer.", "c": [["of the mussaf prayer", "The difference between the first tanna and R. Yehudah — an individual living in a city where there are not ten men. According to the first tanna citing R. Elazar to the effect that it was instituted only with a congregation, this individual is exempt. According to R. Yehudah, an individual is exempt only when he is in a place where there are ten men, in which instance the prayer leader exempts him. The halachah is according to the sages."]]}]];
const MB4_LESSONS=[{"id": "b4-1", "title": "The times of tefillah", "short": "Perek 4 · Mishnah 1", "parts": [0], "phrases": [["תפלת השחר עד חצות", "The morning prayer may be recited until midday."], ["רבי יהודה אומר עד ארבע שעות", "R. Yehudah says: Until the fourth hour."], ["תפלת המנחה עד הערב", "The afternoon prayer may be recited until the evening"], ["רבי יהודה אומר עד פלג המנחה", "R. Yehudah says: Until midway through the day (plag haminchah)."], ["תפלת הערב אין לה קבע", "The evening prayer has no fixed time."], ["ושל מוספין כל היום", "And the mussaf (\"additional\") prayer may be recited the entire day."], ["רבי יהודה אומר עד שבע שעות", "R. Yehudah says: Until the seventh hour."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Until the fourth hour” — For, according to the Rabbis, the daily burnt-offering may be sacrificed until midday; and, according to R. Yehudah, until the fourth hour of the day."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "The morning prayer may be recited until midday.", "tiles": ["תפלת", "השחר", "עד", "חצות"], "decoys": ["היום"], "id": "b4-1-1"}, {"t": "match", "q": "Match each tefillah to its time (Chachamim)", "pairs": [["שחרית", "until chatzos"], ["מנחה", "until the evening"], ["ערבית", "no fixed time"], ["מוסף", "all day"]], "he": true, "id": "b4-1-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "According to R' Yehudah, Shacharis may be said until four hours.", "a": true, "ex": "רבי יהודה אומר עד ארבע שעות.", "id": "b4-1-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“has no fixed time” — Its time is the entire night. It is taught: \"it has no fixed time,\" rather than: \"its time is the entire night,\" for the evening prayer is optional, corresponding, as it does, to the time of the consumption of the limbs and fat-pieces —…"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Yehudah say about Mincha?", "opts": ["Until plag haMincha", "Until midnight", "Until the evening", "All day"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי יהודה אומר עד פלג המנחה.", "id": "b4-1-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "רבי יהודה אומר עד פלג", "after": "", "opts": ["המנחה", "שמוע", "קפנדריא"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי יהודה אומר עד פלג המנחה", "id": "b4-1-5"}]}, {"id": "b4-2", "title": "Tefillah in the beis medrash", "short": "Perek 4 · Mishnah 2–3", "parts": [1, 2], "phrases": [["רבי נחוניה בן הקנה היה מתפלל בכניסתו לבית המדרש וביציאתו תפלה קצרה", "R. Nechuniah b. Hakannah would recite a short prayer upon entering the house of study and upon leaving it."], ["אמרו לו מה מקום לתפלה זו", "When asked: \"What is the place of this prayer?\""], ["אמר להם בכניסתי אני מתפלל שלא תארע תקלה על ידי", "he replied: \"Upon entering I pray that no mischance occur because of me\"; \""], ["וביציאתי אני נותן הודיה על חלקי", "and upon leaving, I give thanks for my portion.\""], ["רבן גמליאל אומר בכל יום מתפלל אדם שמונה עשרה", "R. Gamliel says: One recites eighteen blessings (shemoneh esreh) every day."], ["רבי יהושע אומר מעין שמונה עשרה", "R. Yehoshua says: What is akin to eighteen blessings."], ["ר' עקיבא אומר אם שגורה תפלתו בפיו יתפלל שמונה עשרה ואם לאו מעין שמונה עשרה", "R. Akiva says: If it (the shemoneh esreh) is \"habitual\" in his mouth,, he recites shemoneh esreh; if not, he recites what is akin to it."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“occur because of me” — that I not create a stumbling-block, as explained in the baraitha: \"that I not err in a halachah and my friends rejoice (in my discomfiture)\" — whereby I become the cause of evil, my friends being punished because of me"], "mref": 1}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "R. Nechuniah b. Hakannah would recite a short prayer upon entering the house of study and…", "tiles": ["רבי נחוניה", "בן הקנה", "היה", "מתפלל"], "decoys": ["שמונה"], "id": "b4-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did R' Nechunya pray when entering the beis medrash?", "opts": ["That no mistake should happen through him", "For long life", "For wealth", "For his family"], "a": 0, "ex": "שלא תארע תקלה על ידי.", "id": "b4-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“akin to eighteen blessings” — In the gemara, some explain that he recites each of the middle blessings in short and concludes with the blessing for each one;"], "mref": 2}, {"t": "match", "q": "Match each Tanna to his view", "pairs": [["רבן גמליאל", "שמונה עשרה"], ["רבי יהושע", "מעין שמונה עשרה"], ["ר' עקיבא", "depends if it's fluent"]], "he": true, "id": "b4-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "וביציאתי אני נותן הודיה על", "after": "", "opts": ["חלקי", "ברכו", "המזון"], "a": 0, "ex": "וביציאתי אני נותן הודיה על חלקי", "id": "b4-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b4-3", "title": "A short tefillah", "short": "Perek 4 · Mishnah 4", "parts": [3], "phrases": [["רבי אליעזר אומר העושה תפלתו קבע אין תפלתו תחנונים", "R. Eliezer says: If one makes his prayer k'va, it is not accounted supplication."], ["רבי יהושע אומר המהלך במקום סכנה מתפלל תפלה קצרה", "R. Yehoshua says: One who walks in a place of danger recites a short prayer."], ["אומר הושע השם את עמך את שארית ישראל בכל פרשת העבור יהיו צרכיהם לפניך ברוך אתה ה' שומע תפלה", "He says: \"Help, O L-rd, Your people, the remnant of Israel; bechal parashath haibur, let their needs be before You. Blessed are You, O L-rd, who listens to prayer.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“makes his prayer k'va” — so that his prayer feels burdensome to him. \"k'va\" — \"It is chok kavua (\"a fixed statute\") for me to pray, and I must 'deliver myself' of it.\""], "mref": 3}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "R. Eliezer says: If one makes his prayer k'va, it is not accounted supplication.", "tiles": ["רבי אליעזר", "אומר העושה", "תפלתו", "קבע"], "decoys": ["במקום"], "id": "b4-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Eliezer say about one who makes his tefillah קבע (fixed and rote)?", "opts": ["It is not supplication", "It is the best tefillah", "He must repeat it", "It counts double"], "a": 0, "ex": "העושה תפלתו קבע אין תפלתו תחנונים.", "id": "b4-3-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where does one say the short tefillah?", "opts": ["In a place of danger", "In shul", "At a wedding", "On Shabbos"], "a": 0, "ex": "המהלך במקום סכנה מתפלל תפלה קצרה.", "id": "b4-3-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "רבי יהושע אומר המהלך במקום סכנה מתפלל תפלה", "after": "", "opts": ["קצרה", "מאורי", "עשרה"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי יהושע אומר המהלך במקום סכנה מתפלל תפלה קצרה", "id": "b4-3-4"}]}, {"id": "b4-4", "title": "Facing the Kodesh HaKodashim", "short": "Perek 4 · Mishnah 5–6", "parts": [4, 5], "phrases": [["היה רוכב על החמור ירד", "If he were riding on an ass, he dismounts (to pray)."], ["ואם אינו יכול לירד יחזיר את פניו", "And if he cannot dismount, he turns his face"], ["ואם אינו יכול להחזיר את פניו יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים", "And if he cannot turn his face, he directs his thoughts to the holy of holies"], ["היה יושב בספינה או בקרון או באסדא יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים", "If he were sitting in a boat, in a wagon, or on an asda, he directs his thoughts to the holy of holies."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“he dismounts (to pray)” — The halachah is not in accordance with this anonymous Mishnah; but whether or not he had someone to hold his ass, he does not dismount, for his mind is not settled (enough for prayer) if he must dismount."], "mref": 4}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If he were riding on an ass, he dismounts (to pray).", "tiles": ["היה רוכב", "על", "החמור", "ירד"], "decoys": ["אינו"], "id": "b4-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "If one riding a donkey can't get down to daven, what does he do?", "opts": ["He turns his face (toward the Kodesh HaKodashim)", "He skips Shemoneh Esrei", "He waits until he arrives", "He says only Shema"], "a": 0, "ex": "ואם אינו יכול לירד יחזיר את פניו.", "id": "b4-4-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“or on an asda” — many pieces of wood tied and fastened together, used for sailing on a river. (In Scripture, (II Chronicles 2:15) these are called \"rafsodoth\")"], "mref": 5}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Someone on a boat directs his heart toward the Kodesh HaKodashim.", "a": true, "ex": "יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים.", "id": "b4-4-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ואם אינו יכול להחזיר את פניו יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש", "after": "", "opts": ["הקדשים", "יודע", "מוספין"], "a": 0, "ex": "ואם אינו יכול להחזיר את פניו יכוין את לבו כנגד בית קדש הקדשים", "id": "b4-4-4"}]}, {"id": "b4-5", "title": "Mussaf and the tzibbur", "short": "Perek 4 · Mishnah 7", "parts": [6], "phrases": [["רבי אלעזר בן עזריה אומר אין תפלת המוספין אלא בחבר עיר", "R. Elazar b. Azaryah says: The mussaf (\"additional\") prayer is recited only bechever ir"], ["וחכמים אומרים בחבר עיר ושלא בחבר עיר", "And the sages say: Bechever ir and not bechever ir"], ["רבי יהודה אומר משמו כל מקום שיש חבר עיר היחיד פטור מתפלת המוספין", "R. Yehudah says in his name: Wherever there is a congregation, an individual is exempt from the recitation of the mussaf prayer."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“recited only bechever ir” — bechavurath ha'ir (\"with a company of the city\"); that is, with a congregation, and not individually."], "mref": 6}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "R. Elazar b. Azaryah says: The mussaf (\"additional\") prayer is recited only bechever ir", "tiles": ["רבי אלעזר", "בן עזריה", "אומר", "אין"], "decoys": ["משמו"], "id": "b4-5-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What do the Chachamim say about Mussaf?", "opts": ["It is said with or without a chever ir", "Only with a chever ir", "Only by an individual", "Only on Rosh Chodesh"], "a": 0, "ex": "בחבר עיר ושלא בחבר עיר.", "id": "b4-5-2"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "וחכמים אומרים בחבר עיר ושלא בחבר", "after": "", "opts": ["עיר", "רחץ", "ועבדים"], "a": 0, "ex": "וחכמים אומרים בחבר עיר ושלא בחבר עיר", "id": "b4-5-3"}]}];
const MB5_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "אין עומדין להתפלל אלא מתוך כובד ראש.", "en": "One should not rise to pray except with koved rosh", "c": [["except with koved rosh", "humility and fear, it being written (Psalms 2:11): \"Serve the L-rd with fear\"; and this \"service\" is prayer."]]}, {"he": "חסידים הראשונים היו שוהים שעה אחת ומתפללים כדי שיכונו את לבם למקום.", "en": "The early pietists would abide one hour [in the place where they came to pray] before beginning to pray in order to direct their thoughts to the L-rd.", "c": []}, {"he": "אפילו המלך שואל בשלומו לא ישיבנו.", "en": "Even if the king greets him (while he is praying), he may not answer him.", "c": [["may not answer him", "the king of Israel, specifically; but he does interrupt his prayer for a heathen king, lest he kill him."]]}, {"he": "ואפילו נחש כרוך על עקבו לא יפסיק:", "en": "And even if a snake is wound around his ankle he may not interrupt his prayer.", "c": [["not interrupt his prayer", "a snake, specifically, for in most instances they do not bite; but for a scorpion or an adder, things which certainly bite and kill, he does interrupt it."]]}], [{"he": "מזכירין גבורות גשמים בתחיית המתים.", "en": "Gevuroth geshamim (\"the mightiness of rain\") is mentioned in techiyath hamethim (the resurrection prayer);", "c": [["hamethim (the resurrection prayer)", "Gevuroth geshamim: \"Mashiv haruach,\" which is not an expression of imploration, but of remembrance and praise. It is called \"gevuroth geshamim\" because rain is one of the mighty acts of the Holy One Blessed be He, viz. (Job 9:10): \"He does great things, beyond searching out\"; (Ibid. 5:10): \"He gives rain upon the face of the earth.\""]]}, {"he": "ושואלין הגשמים בברכת השנים.", "en": "and rain is requested in birchath hashanim (the blessing of the years).;", "c": [["and rain is requested", "\"veten tal umatar livracha,\" (which is a request)"], ["blessing of the years)", "Because rain is sustenance, they placed the request for rain in the blessing of sustenance."]]}, {"he": "והבדלה בחונן הדעת.", "en": "and havdalah [at the conclusion of the Sabbath] is recited in chonen hada'ath (\"who bestows knowledge\")", "c": [["hada'ath (\"who bestows knowledge\")", "which is the first weekday blessing. And, in the Yerushalmi: \"Why was havdalah placed in chonen hada'ath? For without knowledge there is no havdalah ('discrimination').\" And this is the halachah."]]}, {"he": "ר' עקיבא אומר אומרה ברכה רביעית בפני עצמה", "en": "R. Akiva says: It is recited individually as the fourth blessing.", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי אליעזר אומר בהודאה:", "en": "R. Eliezer says: It is recited in the thanksgiving benediction.", "c": []}], [{"he": "האומר על קן צפור יגיעו רחמיך ועל טוב יזכר שמך. מודים מודים משתקין אותו.", "en": "If one says: \"To a nest of birds, let Your mercies extend\"; or (if he says): \"For good let Your name be remembered\"; or: \"We thank You,\" \"We thank You\", he is to be silenced.", "c": [["let Your mercies extend", "Just as Your mercies extended to birds and You decreed (Deuteronomy 22:6): \"You shall not take the mother-bird together with the young,\" so be compassionate and merciful to us, he is to be silenced. For he makes the mitzvoth of the Holy One Blessed be He functions of mercy, whereas they are nothing else but decrees of the King to his subjects."], ["Your name be remembered", "the implication being: We shall acknowledge You for good, but not for evil — but we must bless for the evil as well as for the good."], ["You,\" \"We thank You", "the impression being given that two divinities are being accepted. (In the Yerushalmi it is explained that this applies to prayer in a congregation, but in the instance of an individual, it is (warranted) supplication)"]]}, {"he": "העובר לפני התיבה וטעה יעבר אחר תחתיו", "en": "If the prayer leader erred, another should be appointed in his place,", "c": []}, {"he": "ולא יהא סרבן באותה שעה", "en": "and he (the other) should not demur at that time", "c": [["demur at that time", "as one, in general, who is asked to serve as prayer leader, should decline the first request. In this instance, however, he should not decline, for it is demeaning for the prayer to be interrupted that long."]]}, {"he": "מנין הוא מתחיל מתחלת הברכה שטעה בה:", "en": "From which point does he begin? From the beginning of the blessing in which the first one erred.", "c": []}], [{"he": "העובר לפני התיבה לא יענה אחר הכהנים אמן מפני הטירוף", "en": "The prayer leader should not answer Amen after the Cohanim because of teruf (confusion)", "c": [["Amen after the Cohanim", "at the end of each blessing, as the rest of the congregation do"], ["because of teruf (confusion)", "lest he become confused and err. For the prayer leader must begin the next blessing and recite it to them word by word, and if he answered Amen, he could not concentrate and return to the prayer quickly enough and begin the next blessing."]]}, {"he": "ואם אין שם כהן אלא הוא לא ישא את כפיו.", "en": "And if there is no other Cohein but he (the prayer leader), he should not recite the priestly blessing", "c": [["recite the priestly blessing", "lest he not be able to concentrate and return to his prayer to begin \"Sim shalom,\" being distracted by \"awe of the congregation.\""]]}, {"he": "ואם הבטחתו שהוא נושא את כפיו וחוזר לתפלתו רשאי:", "en": "Ve'im havtachato, he is permitted to do so.", "c": [["Ve'im havtachato", "that is, if he is confident (batuach) that he will not be distracted by \"awe of the congregation\""]]}], [{"he": "המתפלל וטעה סימן רע לו.", "en": "If one errs in his prayer, it is a bad sign for him.", "c": []}, {"he": "ואם שליח צבור הוא סימן רע לשולחיו.", "en": "And if he is a prayer leader, it is a bad sign for those who deputed him,", "c": []}, {"he": "מפני ששלוחו של אדם כמותו.", "en": "for a man's deputy is as the man himself.", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו עליו על רבי חנינא בן דוסא כשהיה מתפלל על החולים ואומר זה חי וזה מת.", "en": "They said about R. Chanina b. Dossa that he would pray for the sick, and would say: \"This one will live and this one will die.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמרו לו מנין אתה יודע", "en": "When asked how he knew this,", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר להם אם שגורה תפלתי בפי יודע אני שהוא מקובל ואם לאו יודע אני שהוא מטורף:", "en": "he answered: \"If my prayer is shagur in my mouth, I know that it has been accepted, and if not, I know shehu meturaf\"", "c": [["shagur in my mouth", "ordered and flowing, and I do not stumble in it"], ["I know shehu meturaf", "that the sick one is meturaf (\"torn away\"), as in (Genesis 44:28): \"Surely, he (Joseph) has been torn ('tarof toraf').\" Another interpretation: It may be understood in the sense of (Berachoth 5b): \"Torfim lo tefilato befanav\" (\"His prayer is 'torn up' in his face\"); that is, the prayer that he prayed for the sick one is torn away and taken from him and is not accepted."]]}]];
const MB5_LESSONS=[{"id": "b5-1", "title": "Koved rosh", "short": "Perek 5 · Mishnah 1", "parts": [0], "phrases": [["אין עומדין להתפלל אלא מתוך כובד ראש", "One should not rise to pray except with koved rosh"], ["חסידים הראשונים היו שוהים שעה אחת ומתפללים כדי שיכונו את לבם למקום", "The early pietists would abide one hour before beginning to pray in order to direct their thoughts to the L-rd."], ["אפילו המלך שואל בשלומו לא ישיבנו", "Even if the king greets him (while he is praying), he may not answer him."], ["ואפילו נחש כרוך על עקבו לא יפסיק", "And even if a snake is wound around his ankle he may not interrupt his prayer."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“except with koved rosh” — humility and fear, it being written (Psalms 2:11): \"Serve the L-rd with fear\"; and this \"service\" is prayer."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "One should not rise to pray except with koved rosh", "tiles": ["אין עומדין", "להתפלל אלא", "מתוך", "כובד"], "decoys": ["נחש"], "id": "b5-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did the early chassidim do before davening?", "opts": ["Waited an hour to direct their hearts", "Learned Gemara", "Gave tzedakah", "Said Tehillim"], "a": 0, "ex": "היו שוהים שעה אחת ומתפללים.", "id": "b5-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“may not answer him” — the king of Israel, specifically; but he does interrupt his prayer for a heathen king, lest he kill him."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Even if a king greets him during tefillah, he may not answer.", "a": true, "ex": "אפילו המלך שואל בשלומו לא ישיבנו.", "id": "b5-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "אפילו המלך שואל בשלומו לא", "after": "", "opts": ["ישיבנו", "אלא", "במקום"], "a": 0, "ex": "אפילו המלך שואל בשלומו לא ישיבנו", "id": "b5-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b5-2", "title": "Rain and havdalah", "short": "Perek 5 · Mishnah 2", "parts": [1], "phrases": [["מזכירין גבורות גשמים בתחיית המתים", "Gevuroth geshamim (\"the mightiness of rain\") is mentioned in techiyath hamethim (the resurrection prayer);"], ["ושואלין הגשמים בברכת השנים", "and rain is requested in birchath hashanim (the blessing of the years).;"], ["והבדלה בחונן הדעת", "and havdalah is recited in chonen hada'ath (\"who bestows knowledge\")"], ["ר' עקיבא אומר אומרה ברכה רביעית בפני עצמה", "R. Akiva says: It is recited individually as the fourth blessing."], ["רבי אליעזר אומר בהודאה", "R. Eliezer says: It is recited in the thanksgiving benediction."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“hamethim (the resurrection prayer)” — Gevuroth geshamim: \"Mashiv haruach,\" which is not an expression of imploration, but of remembrance and praise. It is called \"gevuroth geshamim\" because rain is one of the mighty acts of the Holy One Blessed be He, viz."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "Gevuroth geshamim (\"the mightiness of rain\") is mentioned in techiyath hamethim (the…", "tiles": ["מזכירין גבורות", "גשמים", "בתחיית", "המתים"], "decoys": ["אליעזר"], "id": "b5-2-1"}, {"t": "match", "q": "Where is each one said?", "pairs": [["גבורות גשמים", "techiyas hamesim"], ["שאלת גשמים", "birkas hashanim"], ["הבדלה", "chonen hadaas"]], "he": true, "id": "b5-2-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where does R' Akiva say havdalah is said?", "opts": ["As a fourth beracha on its own", "In Modim", "In Retzei", "After Shemoneh Esrei"], "a": 0, "ex": "אומרה ברכה רביעית בפני עצמה.", "id": "b5-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ר' עקיבא אומר אומרה ברכה רביעית בפני", "after": "", "opts": ["עצמה", "בחבר", "ועל"], "a": 0, "ex": "ר' עקיבא אומר אומרה ברכה רביעית בפני עצמה", "id": "b5-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b5-3", "title": "The shaliach tzibbur", "short": "Perek 5 · Mishnah 3–4", "parts": [2, 3], "phrases": [["האומר על קן צפור יגיעו רחמיך ועל טוב יזכר שמך. מודים מודים משתקין אותו", "If one says: \"To a nest of birds, let Your mercies extend\"; or (if he says): \"For good let Your name be remembered\"; or: \"We thank You,\" \"We thank You\", he is to be silenced."], ["העובר לפני התיבה וטעה יעבר אחר תחתיו", "If the prayer leader erred, another should be appointed in his place,"], ["ולא יהא סרבן באותה שעה", "and he (the other) should not demur at that time"], ["מנין הוא מתחיל מתחלת הברכה שטעה בה", "From which point does he begin? From the beginning of the blessing in which the first one erred."], ["העובר לפני התיבה לא יענה אחר הכהנים אמן מפני הטירוף", "The prayer leader should not answer Amen after the Cohanim because of teruf (confusion)"], ["ואם אין שם כהן אלא הוא לא ישא את כפיו", "And if there is no other Cohein but he (the prayer leader), he should not recite the priestly blessing"], ["ואם הבטחתו שהוא נושא את כפיו וחוזר לתפלתו רשאי", "Ve'im havtachato, he is permitted to do so."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“let Your mercies extend” — Just as Your mercies extended to birds and You decreed (Deuteronomy 22:6): \"You shall not take the mother-bird together with the young,\" so be compassionate and merciful to us, he is to be silenced."], "mref": 2}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one says: \"To a nest of birds, let Your mercies extend\"; or (if he says): \"For good…", "tiles": ["האומר על", "קן צפור", "יגיעו", "רחמיך"], "decoys": ["הבטחתו"], "id": "b5-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What is done to one who says 'מודים מודים'?", "opts": ["He is silenced", "He is praised", "He repeats Shemoneh Esrei", "Nothing"], "a": 0, "ex": "משתקין אותו.", "id": "b5-3-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "If the chazzan errs, where does the replacement begin?", "opts": ["From the beginning of the beracha where he erred", "From the beginning of Shemoneh Esrei", "From where he stopped", "From Modim"], "a": 0, "ex": "מתחלת הברכה שטעה בה.", "id": "b5-3-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Amen after the Cohanim” — at the end of each blessing, as the rest of the congregation do"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "tf", "q": "The chazzan should not answer Amen after the kohanim.", "a": true, "ex": "לא יענה אחר הכהנים אמן מפני הטירוף.", "id": "b5-3-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "מנין הוא מתחיל מתחלת הברכה שטעה", "after": "", "opts": ["בה", "מקובל", "כולם"], "a": 0, "ex": "מנין הוא מתחיל מתחלת הברכה שטעה בה", "id": "b5-3-5"}]}, {"id": "b5-4", "title": "R' Chanina ben Dosa", "short": "Perek 5 · Mishnah 5", "parts": [4], "phrases": [["המתפלל וטעה סימן רע לו", "If one errs in his prayer, it is a bad sign for him."], ["ואם שליח צבור הוא סימן רע לשולחיו", "And if he is a prayer leader, it is a bad sign for those who deputed him,"], ["מפני ששלוחו של אדם כמותו", "for a man's deputy is as the man himself."], ["אמרו עליו על רבי חנינא בן דוסא כשהיה מתפלל על החולים ואומר זה חי וזה מת", "They said about R. Chanina b. Dossa that he would pray for the sick, and would say: \"This one will live and this one will die.\""], ["אמרו לו מנין אתה יודע", "When asked how he knew this,"], ["אמר להם אם שגורה תפלתי בפי יודע אני שהוא מקובל ואם לאו יודע אני שהוא מטורף", "he answered: \"If my prayer is shagur in my mouth, I know that it has been accepted, and if not, I know shehu meturaf\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": null, "mref": 4}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one errs in his prayer, it is a bad sign for him.", "tiles": ["המתפלל וטעה", "סימן", "רע", "לו"], "decoys": ["וזה"], "id": "b5-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How did R' Chanina ben Dosa know whether a sick person would live?", "opts": ["If his tefillah flowed fluently", "He saw a dream", "A navi told him", "He asked a doctor"], "a": 0, "ex": "אם שגורה תפלתי בפי יודע אני שהוא מקובל.", "id": "b5-4-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 6, "note": ["Bartenura", "“shagur in my mouth” — ordered and flowing, and I do not stumble in it"], "mref": 4}, {"t": "tf", "q": "A shaliach tzibbur's mistake is a bad sign for those who sent him.", "a": true, "ex": "מפני ששלוחו של אדם כמותו.", "id": "b5-4-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "אמרו עליו על רבי חנינא בן דוסא כשהיה מתפלל על החולים ואומר זה חי וזה", "after": "", "opts": ["מת", "יהודה", "ויאמר"], "a": 0, "ex": "אמרו עליו על רבי חנינא בן דוסא כשהיה מתפלל על החולים ואומר זה חי וזה מת", "id": "b5-4-4"}]}];
const MB6_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "כיצד מברכין על הפירות.", "en": "What blessing does one make over fruits?", "c": []}, {"he": "על פירות האילן אומר בורא פרי העץ.", "en": "On the fruits of the tree he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the tree\" —", "c": []}, {"he": "חוץ מן היין. שעל היין אומר בורא פרי הגפן.", "en": "with the exception of wine, over which he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the vine.\"", "c": [["the exception of wine", "(because of whose distinctiveness, they assigned it a special blessing, as they did with bread)"]]}, {"he": "ועל פירות הארץ אומר בורא פרי האדמה", "en": "On the fruits of the earth he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the earth\" —", "c": []}, {"he": "חוץ מן הפת שעל הפת הוא אומר המוציא לחם מן הארץ.", "en": "with the exception of bread, over which he says: \"Who brings forth bread from the earth.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ועל הירקות אומר בורא פרי האדמה.", "en": "On vegetables he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the earth.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי יהודה אומר בורא מיני דשאים:", "en": "R. Yehudah says: \"Who creates varieties of herbiage.\"", "c": [["creates varieties of herbiage.", "For there are among the fruits of the earth grasses and seeds, such as pulse, and R. Yehudah requires a distinctive blessing for each species. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Yehudah. As to our learning that one says \"Who creates the fruit of the earth\" for vegetables, this applies to vegetables that are generally eaten raw and are eaten raw, or that are generally cooked and are eaten cooked. But for those which are generally eaten raw and are eaten cooked, or which are generally eaten cooked and are eaten raw, he says only \"shehakol.\" And for vegetables which are eaten either raw or cooked, one says \"Who creates the fruit of the earth\" whether he eats them raw or cooked."]]}], [{"he": "ברך על פירות האילן בורא פרי האדמה יצא.", "en": "If one blessed over fruits of the ilan \"Who creates the fruit of the earth,\" he has fulfilled his obligation.", "c": [["has fulfilled his obligation", "An ilan is any growth which when a fruit is taken from it, a shoot remains, and that shoot itself produces fruit in the following year. The blessing for all of its fruits is \"Who creates the fruit of the tree.\" But where, when a fruit is taken, no such shoot remains, the blessing for the fruits is \"Who creates the fruit of the earth.\""]]}, {"he": "ועל פירות הארץ בורא פרי העץ לא יצא.", "en": "And if one blessed over fruits of the earth \"Who creates the fruit of the tree,\" he has not fulfilled his obligation.", "c": []}, {"he": "על כולם אם אמר שהכל נהיה יצא:", "en": "With all foods, if one said \"Who caused all to be\" (\"shehakol\"), he has fulfilled his obligation", "c": [["has fulfilled his obligation", "even for bread and wine. But ab initio, one should not eat any food if he does not know the appropriate blessing."]]}], [{"he": "על דבר שאין גדולו מן הארץ אומר שהכל.", "en": "Over something which does not grow in the ground, one says \"shehakol.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "על החומץ ועל הנובלות ועל הגובאי אומר שהכל.", "en": "Over vinegar, novloth and govai [ritually clean hoppers], one says \"shehakol.\"", "c": [["Over vinegar, novloth", "fruits fallen from the tree before they are fully ripe"]]}, {"he": "על החלב ועל הגבינה ועל הביצים אומר שהכל.", "en": "Over milk, cheese, and eggs, one says \"shehakol.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר כל שהוא מין קללה אין מברכין עליו:", "en": "R. Yehudah says: No blessing is made over anything which is \"species of a curse.\"", "c": [["species of a curse.", "Novloth and govai come through a curse. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Yehudah."]]}], [{"he": "היו לפניו מינים הרבה.", "en": "If there were before him many species,", "c": []}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר אם יש ביניהם ממין שבעה מברך עליו.", "en": "R. Yehudah says: If any of the seven species were among them, he blesses upon them (first).", "c": [["of the seven species", "wheat, barley, grape, fig, pomegranate, olive, date"], ["blesses upon them (first)", "These take precedence, Eretz Yisrael having been graced with them."]]}, {"he": "וחכמים אומרים מברך על איזה מהם שירצה:", "en": "The sages say: He blesses on whichever he wishes,", "c": [["on whichever he wishes", "personal taste taking precedence. The halachah is in accordance with the sages."]]}], [{"he": "ברך על היין שלפני המזון פטר את היין שלאחר המזון", "en": "If one blessed on wine before the meal, he exempts (from blessing) the wine after the meal.", "c": [["wine after the meal", "This applies to Sabbaths and festivals, when the meal is \"appointed\" over the wine following the meal. But on other days, when such \"appointment\" does not obtain, the wine before the meal does not exempt the wine after. Every \"after the meal\" in our Mishnah means after they have finished with the bread, before reciting grace."]]}, {"he": "ברך על הפרפרת שלפני המזון פטר את הפרפרת שלאחר המזון.", "en": "If he blessed over the parpereth before the meal, he exempts the parpereth after the meal.", "c": [["parpereth after the meal", "Parpereth is anything which accompanies the bread, such as meat, eggs, and fish. Sometimes they would bring parperaoth before the meal to whet the appetite, and again, after the meal, after having finished with the bread."]]}, {"he": "ברך על הפת פטר את הפרפרת.", "en": "The blessing over the bread exempts the parpereth.", "c": []}, {"he": "על הפרפרת לא פטר את הפת.", "en": "The blessing over parpereth does not exempt the bread.", "c": []}, {"he": "בית שמאי אומרים אף לא מעשה קדרה:", "en": "Beth Shammai say: It also does not exempt what comes from the pot", "c": [["comes from the pot", "such as grits, fruit, green grain, and flour cooked in water, such as pancakes and the like. And there are some who understand the \"parpereth\" of our Mishnah as loaf hardened in a dish, which does not have the appearance of bread, for which the blessing is borei minei mezonoth. This explains the necessity of \"The blessing over the parpereth does not exempt that over the bread\" — even though parpereth, too, is a kind of bread. But it does exempt \"what comes from the pot.\" And Beth Shammai hold that just as the blessing over parpereth does not exempt the bread, so it does not exempt what comes from the pot. The halachah is not in accordance with Beth Shammai."]]}], [{"he": "היו יושבין לאכול כל אחד ואחד מברך לעצמו.", "en": "If they sat down to eat, each one blesses for himself,", "c": [["sat down to eat", "without reclining, a sign that they had not arranged to eat together, for when groups of people had arranged to eat together, they would recline on mats, and eat and drink reclining on their left side"], ["one blesses for himself", "there being no \"appointed\" meal without reclining. However, if they said: \"Let us go and eat bread in that place,\" even if they did not recline, it is as if they had, and one blesses for all; and they also join together for grace."]]}, {"he": "הסיבו אחד מברך לכולן.", "en": "If they reclined, one blesses for all.", "c": []}, {"he": "בא להם יין בתוך המזון כל אחד ואחד מברך לעצמו. לאחר המזון אחד מברך לכולם.", "en": "If wine were brought before them during the meal, each one blesses (over the wine) for himself", "c": [["the wine) for himself", "since their throat is not free, and the recliners are intent not upon the blessing, but upon swallowing what is in their mouths. Or it may be that we are apprehensive of their choking in answering Amen."]]}, {"he": "והוא אומר על המוגמר אף על פי שאין מביאין את המוגמר אלא לאחר הסעודה:", "en": "And he makes the blessing over the mugmar, even though the mugmar is not brought until after the meal", "c": [["blessing over the mugmar", "The one who makes grace blesses over the mugmar: \"Who creates woods of spices.\" And even though there may be present a person more eminent than he, since he began with one (blessing), he makes the other"], ["until after the meal", "after grace, so that it is not a requirement of the meal. Still, since he began the latter blessings, he completes them. [\"Mugmar\": After the meal they were wont to bring wood-spices on a coal-pan, to produce an aromatic fragrance."]]}], [{"he": "הביאו לפניו מליח בתחלה ופת עמו מברך על המליח ופוטר את הפת שהפת טפלה לו", "en": "If they brought before him maliach [anything maluach (salted)] in the beginning, and bread with it, he blesses over the maliach and exempts the bread; for the bread is ancillary to it.", "c": [["is ancillary to it", "One who had a large helping of especially sweet fruits eats something salty afterwards to \"break\" the sweetness in his body. And because he cannot eat the maliach by itself, he eats some bread with it. But the maliach by itself is primary, and the bread is ancillary to it."]]}, {"he": "זה הכלל כל שהוא עיקר ועמו טפלה. מברך על העיקר ופוטר את הטפלה:", "en": "This is the rule: In every instance of primary and ancillary, one blesses on the primary and exempts the ancillary.", "c": []}], [{"he": "אכל תאנים וענבים ורמונים מברך אחריהן שלש ברכות דברי רבן גמליאל.", "en": "If one ate figs, grapes, or pomegranates, he makes three blessings afterwards. These are the words of R. Gamliel.", "c": [["words of R. Gamliel", "One makes three blessings after any of the seven varieties, R. Gamliel holding that \"And you shall eat, and you shall be sated, and you shall bless\" (Deuteronomy 8:10) refers not to bread alone, but to all of the seven varieties mentioned above in that section (Ibid. 8). And in this verse, three blessings are intimated: \"And you shall bless\" — \"hazan\"; \"for the land\" — the blessing for the land; \"the good\" — \"who builds Jerusalem,\" viz. (Deuteronomy 3:25): \"this goodly mountain.\""]]}, {"he": "וחכמים אומרים ברכה אחת מעין שלש", "en": "And the sages say: One blessing, like three", "c": [["One blessing, like three", "i.e., like three blessings. If he ate grapes, figs, pomegranates, olives, and dates, he blesses \"for the tree, and for the fruit of the tree, and for the good, desirable land, etc.\", and he concludes: \"for the land and for the fruits.\" And in Eretz Yisrael, he concludes: \"for the land and for its fruits.\" And he recites this blessing itself for wine, but begins: \"for the vine and for the fruit of the vine.\" And for all things made from the five types of grain, instead of \"for the tree and for the fruit of the tree,\" he says: \"for the food and for the sustenance,\" and he concludes: \"for the land and for the food.\""]]}, {"he": "רבי עקיבא אומר אפילו אכל שלק והוא מזונו מברך אחריו שלש ברכות.", "en": "R. Akiva says: Even if he ate shelek [boiled vegetables] and that is his food [i.e., his staple], he recites three blessings afterwards,", "c": [["recites three blessings afterwards", "for \"And you shall eat and you shall be sated\" applies to anything one eats. And the halachah is in accordance with the sages, that three blessings are recited only for bread. And for the seven varieties, \"one blessing like three,\" and on all other things: \"Borei nefashoth rabboth vechesronan\" (\"He creates many creatures and (supplies) their lacks\"). \"their lacks\" — such as bread and water, without which it is impossible to survive. \"And for all that He created to sustain the spirit of all living things\" — that is, for everything in the world, which, even if it had not been created, the creatures could survive without, and which was created only to provide pleasure and additional good. And because this blessing contains two elements, it is a long blessing, which opens and closes with \"Baruch,\" as stated in Yerushalmi, the closing being: \"Blessed (Baruch) are you, O L-rd, Life of the worlds.\""]]}, {"he": "השותה מים לצמאו אומר שהכל נהיה בדברו.", "en": "If one drinks water to assuage his thirst [specifically] he says \"shehakol nihyeh bidvaro\" (\"All came into being through His word\").", "c": [["being through His word\")", "But if one drinks water to swallow something stuck in his throat and the like, he does not bless."]]}, {"he": "ר' טרפון אומר בורא נפשות רבות:", "en": "R. Tarfon says: \"Borei nefashoth rabboth.\"", "c": [["says: \"Borei nefashoth rabboth.", "He recites this before drinking water. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Tarfon; but before drinking water he says \"shehakol,\" and after, \"Borei nefashoth rabboth.\""]]}]];
const MB6_LESSONS=[{"id": "b6-1", "title": "Which beracha?", "short": "Perek 6 · Mishnah 1", "parts": [0], "phrases": [["כיצד מברכין על הפירות", "What blessing does one make over fruits?"], ["על פירות האילן אומר בורא פרי העץ", "On the fruits of the tree he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the tree\" —"], ["חוץ מן היין. שעל היין אומר בורא פרי הגפן", "with the exception of wine, over which he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the vine.\""], ["ועל פירות הארץ אומר בורא פרי האדמה", "On the fruits of the earth he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the earth\" —"], ["חוץ מן הפת שעל הפת הוא אומר המוציא לחם מן הארץ", "with the exception of bread, over which he says: \"Who brings forth bread from the earth.\""], ["ועל הירקות אומר בורא פרי האדמה", "On vegetables he says: \"Who creates the fruit of the earth.\""], ["רבי יהודה אומר בורא מיני דשאים", "R. Yehudah says: \"Who creates varieties of herbiage.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“the exception of wine” — (because of whose distinctiveness, they assigned it a special blessing, as they did with bread)"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "What blessing does one make over fruits?", "tiles": ["כיצד", "מברכין", "על", "הפירות"], "decoys": ["הגפן"], "id": "b6-1-1"}, {"t": "match", "q": "Match the food to its beracha", "pairs": [["פירות האילן", "בורא פרי העץ"], ["יין", "בורא פרי הגפן"], ["פירות הארץ", "בורא פרי האדמה"], ["פת", "המוציא לחם מן הארץ"]], "he": true, "id": "b6-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“creates varieties of herbiage.” — For there are among the fruits of the earth grasses and seeds, such as pulse, and R. Yehudah requires a distinctive blessing for each species. The halachah is not in accordance with R. Yehudah."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Yehudah say on vegetables?", "opts": ["בורא מיני דשאים", "בורא פרי העץ", "שהכל", "המוציא"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי יהודה אומר בורא מיני דשאים.", "id": "b6-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ועל פירות הארץ אומר בורא פרי", "after": "", "opts": ["האדמה", "אמר", "יהודה"], "a": 0, "ex": "ועל פירות הארץ אומר בורא פרי האדמה", "id": "b6-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b6-2", "title": "Mistakes, and shehakol", "short": "Perek 6 · Mishnah 2–3", "parts": [1, 2], "phrases": [["ברך על פירות האילן בורא פרי האדמה יצא", "If one blessed over fruits of the ilan \"Who creates the fruit of the earth,\" he has fulfilled his obligation."], ["ועל פירות הארץ בורא פרי העץ לא יצא", "And if one blessed over fruits of the earth \"Who creates the fruit of the tree,\" he has not fulfilled his obligation."], ["על כולם אם אמר שהכל נהיה יצא", "With all foods, if one said \"Who caused all to be\" (\"shehakol\"), he has fulfilled his obligation"], ["על דבר שאין גדולו מן הארץ אומר שהכל", "Over something which does not grow in the ground, one says \"shehakol.\""], ["על החומץ ועל הנובלות ועל הגובאי אומר שהכל", "Over vinegar, novloth and govai, one says \"shehakol.\""], ["על החלב ועל הגבינה ועל הביצים אומר שהכל", "Over milk, cheese, and eggs, one says \"shehakol.\""], ["ר' יהודה אומר כל שהוא מין קללה אין מברכין עליו", "R. Yehudah says: No blessing is made over anything which is \"species of a curse.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“has fulfilled his obligation” — An ilan is any growth which when a fruit is taken from it, a shoot remains, and that shoot itself produces fruit in the following year."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one blessed over fruits of the ilan \"Who creates the fruit of the earth,\" he has…", "tiles": ["ברך על", "פירות האילן", "בורא", "פרי"], "decoys": ["מברכין"], "id": "b6-2-1"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "If one said בורא פרי העץ on vegetables, he fulfilled his obligation.", "a": false, "ex": "ועל פירות הארץ בורא פרי העץ לא יצא.", "id": "b6-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Over vinegar, novloth” — fruits fallen from the tree before they are fully ripe"], "mref": 2}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Which beracha is said on milk, cheese and eggs?", "opts": ["שהכל", "בורא פרי האדמה", "בורא פרי העץ", "המוציא"], "a": 0, "ex": "על החלב ועל הגבינה ועל הביצים אומר שהכל.", "id": "b6-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "על דבר שאין גדולו מן הארץ אומר", "after": "", "opts": ["שהכל", "שמע", "ישראל"], "a": 0, "ex": "על דבר שאין גדולו מן הארץ אומר שהכל", "id": "b6-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b6-3", "title": "Which food first", "short": "Perek 6 · Mishnah 4–5", "parts": [3, 4], "phrases": [["היו לפניו מינים הרבה", "If there were before him many species,"], ["ר' יהודה אומר אם יש ביניהם ממין שבעה מברך עליו", "R. Yehudah says: If any of the seven species were among them, he blesses upon them (first)."], ["וחכמים אומרים מברך על איזה מהם שירצה", "The sages say: He blesses on whichever he wishes,"], ["ברך על היין שלפני המזון פטר את היין שלאחר המזון", "If one blessed on wine before the meal, he exempts (from blessing) the wine after the meal."], ["ברך על הפרפרת שלפני המזון פטר את הפרפרת שלאחר המזון", "If he blessed over the parpereth before the meal, he exempts the parpereth after the meal."], ["ברך על הפת פטר את הפרפרת", "The blessing over the bread exempts the parpereth."], ["על הפרפרת לא פטר את הפת", "The blessing over parpereth does not exempt the bread."], ["בית שמאי אומרים אף לא מעשה קדרה", "Beth Shammai say: It also does not exempt what comes from the pot"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“of the seven species” — wheat, barley, grape, fig, pomegranate, olive, date"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If there were before him many species,", "tiles": ["היו", "לפניו", "מינים", "הרבה"], "decoys": ["ברך"], "id": "b6-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "With many foods in front of him, which does R' Yehudah bless first?", "opts": ["One of the seven species", "The biggest", "The one he likes most", "Bread"], "a": 0, "ex": "אם יש ביניהם ממין שבעה מברך עליו.", "id": "b6-3-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "A beracha on bread covers the parperes (side dishes).", "a": true, "ex": "ברך על הפת פטר את הפרפרת.", "id": "b6-3-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 8, "note": ["Bartenura", "“wine after the meal” — This applies to Sabbaths and festivals, when the meal is \"appointed\" over the wine following the meal. But on other days, when such \"appointment\" does not obtain, the wine before the meal does not exempt the wine after."], "mref": 4}, {"t": "tf", "q": "A beracha on the parperes covers the bread.", "a": false, "ex": "על הפרפרת לא פטר את הפת.", "id": "b6-3-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ברך על הפרפרת שלפני המזון פטר את הפרפרת שלאחר", "after": "", "opts": ["המזון", "ביציאתו", "בתוך"], "a": 0, "ex": "ברך על הפרפרת שלפני המזון פטר את הפרפרת שלאחר המזון", "id": "b6-3-5"}]}, {"id": "b6-4", "title": "Eating together; main and secondary", "short": "Perek 6 · Mishnah 6–7", "parts": [5, 6], "phrases": [["היו יושבין לאכול כל אחד ואחד מברך לעצמו", "If they sat down to eat, each one blesses for himself,"], ["הסיבו אחד מברך לכולן", "If they reclined, one blesses for all."], ["בא להם יין בתוך המזון כל אחד ואחד מברך לעצמו. לאחר המזון אחד מברך לכולם", "If wine were brought before them during the meal, each one blesses (over the wine) for himself"], ["והוא אומר על המוגמר אף על פי שאין מביאין את המוגמר אלא לאחר הסעודה", "And he makes the blessing over the mugmar, even though the mugmar is not brought until after the meal"], ["הביאו לפניו מליח בתחלה ופת עמו מברך על המליח ופוטר את הפת שהפת טפלה לו", "If they brought before him maliach in the beginning, and bread with it, he blesses over the maliach and exempts the bread; for the bread is ancillary to it."], ["זה הכלל כל שהוא עיקר ועמו טפלה. מברך על העיקר ופוטר את הטפלה", "This is the rule: In every instance of primary and ancillary, one blesses on the primary and exempts the ancillary."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“sat down to eat” — without reclining, a sign that they had not arranged to eat together, for when groups of people had arranged to eat together, they would recline on mats, and eat and drink reclining on their left side"], "mref": 5}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If they sat down to eat, each one blesses for himself,", "tiles": ["היו יושבין", "לאכול כל", "אחד", "ואחד"], "decoys": ["לאחר"], "id": "b6-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "When they recline together at a meal, who makes the beracha?", "opts": ["One person for everyone", "Each person for himself", "The youngest", "No one"], "a": 0, "ex": "הסיבו אחד מברך לכולן.", "id": "b6-4-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 6, "note": ["Bartenura", "“is ancillary to it” — One who had a large helping of especially sweet fruits eats something salty afterwards to \"break\" the sweetness in his body. And because he cannot eat the maliach by itself, he eats some bread with it."], "mref": 6}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What is the rule of עיקר and טפל?", "opts": ["Bless the main food; it covers the secondary one", "Bless each food separately", "Bless the secondary food first", "Only bread needs a beracha"], "a": 0, "ex": "מברך על העיקר ופוטר את הטפלה.", "id": "b6-4-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "והוא אומר על המוגמר אף על פי שאין מביאין את המוגמר אלא לאחר", "after": "", "opts": ["הסעודה", "הרעמים", "חייב"], "a": 0, "ex": "והוא אומר על המוגמר אף על פי שאין מביאין את המוגמר אלא לאחר הסעודה", "id": "b6-4-4"}]}, {"id": "b6-5", "title": "Berachos after eating", "short": "Perek 6 · Mishnah 8", "parts": [7], "phrases": [["אכל תאנים וענבים ורמונים מברך אחריהן שלש ברכות דברי רבן גמליאל", "If one ate figs, grapes, or pomegranates, he makes three blessings afterwards. These are the words of R. Gamliel."], ["וחכמים אומרים ברכה אחת מעין שלש", "And the sages say: One blessing, like three"], ["רבי עקיבא אומר אפילו אכל שלק והוא מזונו מברך אחריו שלש ברכות", "R. Akiva says: Even if he ate shelek and that is his food, he recites three blessings afterwards,"], ["השותה מים לצמאו אומר שהכל נהיה בדברו", "If one drinks water to assuage his thirst he says \"shehakol nihyeh bidvaro\" (\"All came into being through His word\")."], ["ר' טרפון אומר בורא נפשות רבות", "R. Tarfon says: \"Borei nefashoth rabboth.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“words of R. Gamliel” — One makes three blessings after any of the seven varieties, R. Gamliel holding that \"And you shall eat, and you shall be sated, and you shall bless\" (Deuteronomy 8:10) refers not to bread alone, but to all of the seven varieties mentioned…"], "mref": 7}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one ate figs, grapes, or pomegranates, he makes three blessings afterwards. These are…", "tiles": ["אכל תאנים", "וענבים ורמונים", "מברך", "אחריהן"], "decoys": ["טרפון"], "id": "b6-5-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What do the Chachamim say one says after figs, grapes and pomegranates?", "opts": ["One beracha that is like three", "Three berachos", "No beracha", "Shehakol"], "a": 0, "ex": "ברכה אחת מעין שלש.", "id": "b6-5-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“being through His word\")” — But if one drinks water to swallow something stuck in his throat and the like, he does not bless."], "mref": 7}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Tarfon say on water?", "opts": ["בורא נפשות רבות", "שהכל נהיה בדברו", "בורא פרי העץ", "No beracha"], "a": 0, "ex": "ר' טרפון אומר בורא נפשות רבות.", "id": "b6-5-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "רבי עקיבא אומר אפילו אכל שלק והוא מזונו מברך אחריו שלש", "after": "", "opts": ["ברכות", "שתים", "בנה"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי עקיבא אומר אפילו אכל שלק והוא מזונו מברך אחריו שלש ברכות", "id": "b6-5-4"}]}];
const MB7_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "שלשה שאכלו כאחת חייבין לזמן", "en": "Three who ate together chayavin lezamen.", "c": [["ate together chayavin lezamen", "They must \"group\" (lehizdamen) together to bless in the plural: \"Let us bless Him of whose fare we have eaten.\""]]}, {"he": "אכל דמאי ומעשר ראשון שנטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שנפדו והשמש שאכל כזית והכותי מזמנין עליהם.", "en": "A zimun (such a group) is made (even) if one ate: demai, and ma'aser rishon (the first tithe) whose terumah had been taken, and ma'aser sheni (the second tithe) and hekdesh (devoted objects) which were redeemed, and (a zimun is made with) the waiter who ate an olive-size., and (with) a Cuthite", "c": [["if one ate: demai", "The fruits of an am ha'aretz (an unlearned person) are called \"demai,\" i.e., \"da mai?\" \"What is this?\" Tithed or untithed? For amei ha'aretz are suspect in respect to tithes. And the sages forbade eating of their fruits until they were tithed. But if one did eat of them without tithing, the blessing (grace) is, nonetheless, recited, and it is not considered \"a mitzvah coming through a transgression\" because most amei ha'aretz do tithe"], ["terumah had been taken", "even though terumah gedolah (\"the great terumah\") had not been taken of it. To wit: a Levite preceded a Cohein and took his ma'aser in the stalks, before the Cohein had taken terumah gedolah. The Cohein was to have taken terumah gedolah, one-fiftieth, first, the Torah calling it \"reshith\" (\"the first\"). It emerges, then, that the terumah gedolah of the Cohein is found in this ma'aser — one fiftieth of it — aside from terumath ma'aser, it being incumbent upon the Levite to separate terumah from his ma'aser. Our Mishnah apprises us that the Levite need not separate terumah gedolah from it, it being written (Numbers 18:26): \"Then you (the Levites) shall separate from it terumah for the L-rd, ma'aser from the ma'aser\" — ma'aser from the ma'aser, and not terumah gedolah and terumath ma'aser of the ma'aser."], ["objects) which were redeemed", "as when he gave the principal, but not the fifth (the owners adding a fifth), the tanna apprising us that the (absence of) the fifth does not stand in the way (of the blessing)."], ["who ate an olive-size", "for we would think that since the waiter had no fixed place, but comes and goes, a zimun is not made with him; we are, therefore, apprised otherwise. In all of these instances we are apprised that though they are similar to what is forbidden, they do not constitute \"blessing coming through transgression.\""], ["and (with) a Cuthite", "one of the sect of idolators that the king of Ashur brought from Cutha and from other lands and settled in the cities of Shomron. They became proselytes from fear of the lions which started to devour them, as explained in II Kings (17), and they observed the written Law, being more fastidious than the Jews themselves in the observance of every mitzvah that they kept. They were, therefore, trusted in respect to certain mitzvoth until they were found to have set up an image of a dove on the top of Mount Gerizim, which they served. From that time on they were regarded as absolute idolators in every respect, for which reason today a zimun is not made with a Cuthite."]]}, {"he": "אבל אכל טבל ומעשר ראשון שלא נטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שלא נפדו והשמש שאכל פחות מכזית והנכרי אין מזמנין עליהם:", "en": "But a zimun is not made if one ate tevel, and ma'aser rishon whose terumah had not been taken., and ma'aser sheni and hekdesh which had not been redeemed, and (with) the waiter who ate less than an olive-size., and an idolator.", "c": [["if one ate tevel", "Grain from which terumah and ma'aser were not taken is called \"tevel,\" (\"tav lo\" - \"It is not good\"). And not only (it goes without saying) is a zimun not made over what is tevel according to Scripture, but even over what is tevel by rabbinical ordinance, such as grain grown in an unperforated flower pot."], ["had not been taken", "\"Terumah\" here is not terumath ma'aser, for that would be absolute tevel, but the instance referred to is one in which the Levite preceded the Cohein to the pile after it had been finished off and become subject to terumah according to the Torah, and took ma'aser rishon first. One-fiftieth of that is subject to the Cohein's terumah gedolah; and so long as the terumah gedolah has not been separated, even though the terumah of ma'aser has been separated, no zimun is made over it. (If the Levite had preceded the Cohein and taken his ma'aser in the stalks, before the finishing off of the pile, there would be no need of separating terumah gedolah, as explained above)."], ["had not been redeemed", "It need not be stated that (no zimun is made) if they had not been redeemed at all; for this goes without saying. The reference is, rather, to an instance in which it had been redeemed, but not according to the halachah, as when ma'aser sheni is redeemed with fragments of silver or with a coin which has no design on it, Scripture having stated (Deuteronomy 14:25): \"Vetzarta the money\" — money that has a tzura (design on it); and as when hekdesh is redeemed with land instead of with money, Scripture having stated (Leviticus 27:19): \"Then he shall add one-fifth of the money.\""], ["less than an olive-size", "This is a superfluous Mishnah; but since most (of the aforementioned instances) are repeated for a necessary teaching, this, too, is repeated."], ["and an idolator", "The reference is to a proselyte who underwent circumcision but not ritual immersion, the Mishnah apprising us that as long as he has not undergone ritual immersion he is still an idolator, not being considered a proselyte until he has undergone both circumcision and ritual immersion."]]}], [{"he": "נשים ועבדים וקטנים אין מזמנין עליהם.", "en": "Women and minors are not counted in a zimun.", "c": [["counted in a zimun", "Only minors who do not know to whom they are blessing; but a minor who does know is counted in a zimun. And there are some of our rabbis who say that they said this (\"a minor who does know, etc.\") only in respect to a boy aged thirteen years and one day, who did not yet develop two (pubic) hairs, such a boy being called \"katan poreach\" (see Berachoth 47b); but a younger boy is not counted for a zimun even if he does know to whom he is blessing. And in Yerushalmi they state as halachah that a minor is not counted for a zimun at all, until he becomes an adult (i.e., thirteen) and shows two hairs. Women form a zimun for themselves and bondsmen for themselves, but not together, because of (apprehension of) promiscuity."]]}, {"he": "עד כמה מזמנין עד כזית ר' יהודה אומר עד כביצה:", "en": "What is the (minimum) amount (of food) required for a zimun? An olive-size. R. Yehudah says: An egg-size.", "c": [["a zimun? An olive-size", "This is the halachah, and not as R. Yehudah says."]]}], [{"he": "כיצד מזמנין בשלשה אומר נברך. בשלשה והוא אומר ברכו.", "en": "How does one bless in a zimun? With three, he says: \"Let us bless.\" With three and himself, he says: \"Bless.\"", "c": [["himself, he says: \"Bless.", "For there is a zimun without him; and thus with all."]]}, {"he": "בעשרה אומר נברך לאלקינו. בעשרה והוא אומר ברכו. אחד עשרה ואחד עשרה רבוא.", "en": "With ten he says: \"Let us bless our G-d.\" (And the same is true for) eleven and eleven myriads.", "c": [["eleven and eleven myriads", "This first section is as per R. Akiva, who says that we do here (with zimun) as we do in the house of prayer. When the number reaches ten, it makes no difference whether there are many or few beyond that; here, too, there is no difference."]]}, {"he": "במאה אומר נברך לה' אלקינו. במאה והוא אומר ברכו.", "en": "With a hundred, he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d.\" With a hundred and himself he says: \"Bless.\"", "c": [["the L-rd our G-d.", "This second section is all as per R. Yossi Haglili, who says: \"They bless according to the numerousness of the congregation, it being written (Psalms 68:27): 'In congregations bless G-d.'\" And the halachah is that from three until, but not including, ten, the one reciting the blessing says: \"Let us bless Him of whose fare we have eaten,\" and all respond: \"Blessed be He of whose fare we have eaten and through whose good we live.\" From ten and above, the one reciting the blessing says: \"Let us bless our G-d, of whose fare we have eaten,\" and all respond: \"Blessed be our G-d, of whose fare we have eaten and through whose good we live.\""]]}, {"he": "באלף אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל. באלף והוא אומר ברכו.", "en": "With a thousand he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel.\" With a thousand and himself he says: \"Bless.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ברבוא אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו. ברבוא והוא אומר ברכו.", "en": "With ten thousand he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel, the G-d of hosts, the Dweller among the cherubs, for the fare that we have eaten.\" With ten thousand and himself he says: \"Bless.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "כענין שהוא מברך כך עונין אחריו ברוך ה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו.", "en": "In the manner that he blesses, so the others respond: \"Blessed be the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel, the G-d of hosts, the Dweller among the cherubs, for the fare that we have eaten.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ר' יוסי הגלילי אומר לפי רוב הקהל הן מברכין שנאמר (תהלים סח, כז) במקהלות ברכו אלקים ה' ממקור ישראל.", "en": "R. Yossi says: They bless according to the numerousness of the congregation, it being written (Psalms 68:7): 'In congregations bless G-d, the L-rd from the source of Israel.'\"", "c": []}, {"he": "אמר רבי עקיבא מה מצינו בבית הכנסת אחד מרובין ואחד מועטין אומר ברכו את ה'.", "en": "R. Akiva said: (We do with zimun) as we do in the house of prayer. Whether there are many or few, he says: \"Bless the L-rd.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "רבי ישמעאל אומר ברכו את ה' המבורך:", "en": "R. Yishmael says: \"Bless the L-rd, who is blessed.\"", "c": [["L-rd, who is blessed.", "And the halachah is in accordance with R. Yishmael."]]}], [{"he": "שלשה שאכלו כאחד אינן רשאין ליחלק וכן ארבעה וכן חמשה.", "en": "If three ate together, they are not permitted to separate,. And the same applies to four or five.", "c": [["not permitted to separate", "having become subject to the obligation of zimun"], ["to four or five", "Three are not permitted to make the zimun and one to separate, he, too, having become subject to the obligation of zimun."]]}, {"he": "ששה נחלקין עד עשרה ועשרה אינן נחלקין עד שיהיו עשרים:", "en": "Six may separate, until ten; but ten may not separate, until there are twenty,.", "c": [["Six may separate", "(three) for zimun in one group and three) in another"], ["ten may not separate", "their having become subject to zimun with mentioning of the Name"], ["until there are twenty", "at which time they may separate into two groups (of ten) if they wish"]]}], [{"he": "שתי חבורות שהיו אוכלות בבית אחד בזמן שמקצתן רואין אלו את אלו הרי אלו מצטרפים לזמון", "en": "Two groups who ate in one house — if some of them see each other, they join for zimun;", "c": []}, {"he": "ואם לאו אלו מזמנין לעצמן ואלו מזמנין לעצמן", "en": "and if not, each group makes a zimun itself.", "c": [["makes a zimun itself", "And if one waiter serves both groups, though they do not see each other, the waiter joins them."]]}, {"he": "אין מברכין על היין עד שיתן לתוכו מים דברי רבי אליעזר.", "en": "One may not make the blessing over wine [borei p'ri hagafen] until he dilutes it with water. These are the words of R. Eliezer.", "c": [["words of R. Eliezer", "For their wine was very strong and was not fit for drinking until it was diluted. Therefore, (before being diluted) it was not \"changed for the better\" and did not depart from its original blessing, \"borei p'ri ha'etz,\" for grapes. But the halachah is not in accordance with R. Eliezer."]]}, {"he": "וחכמים אומרים מברכין:", "en": "And the sages say: One does make the blessing.", "c": []}]];
const MB7_LESSONS=[{"id": "b7-1", "title": "Zimun", "short": "Perek 7 · Mishnah 1–2", "parts": [0, 1], "phrases": [["שלשה שאכלו כאחת חייבין לזמן", "Three who ate together chayavin lezamen."], ["אכל דמאי ומעשר ראשון שנטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שנפדו והשמש שאכל כזית והכותי מזמנין עליהם", "A zimun (such a group) is made (even) if one ate: demai, and ma'aser rishon (the first tithe) whose terumah had been taken, and ma'aser sheni (the second tithe) and hekdesh (devoted objects) which were redeemed, and (a zimun is made with) the waiter who ate an olive-size., and (with) a Cuthite"], ["אבל אכל טבל ומעשר ראשון שלא נטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שלא נפדו והשמש שאכל פחות מכזית והנכרי אין מזמנין עליהם", "But a zimun is not made if one ate tevel, and ma'aser rishon whose terumah had not been taken., and ma'aser sheni and hekdesh which had not been redeemed, and (with) the waiter who ate less than an olive-size., and an idolator."], ["נשים ועבדים וקטנים אין מזמנין עליהם", "Women and minors are not counted in a zimun."], ["עד כמה מזמנין עד כזית ר' יהודה אומר עד כביצה", "What is the (minimum) amount (of food) required for a zimun? An olive-size. R. Yehudah says: An egg-size."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“ate together chayavin lezamen” — They must \"group\" (lehizdamen) together to bless in the plural: \"Let us bless Him of whose fare we have eaten.\""], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "Three who ate together chayavin lezamen.", "tiles": ["שלשה שאכלו", "כאחת", "חייבין", "לזמן"], "decoys": ["אבל"], "id": "b7-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How many who ate together must make a zimun?", "opts": ["Three", "Two", "Ten", "Seven"], "a": 0, "ex": "שלשה שאכלו כאחת חייבין לזמן.", "id": "b7-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“counted in a zimun” — Only minors who do not know to whom they are blessing; but a minor who does know is counted in a zimun."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Yehudah say is the minimum amount for zimun?", "opts": ["A k'beitzah (an egg's size)", "A k'zayis", "A full meal", "Any amount"], "a": 0, "ex": "ר' יהודה אומר עד כביצה.", "id": "b7-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "אבל אכל טבל ומעשר ראשון שלא נטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שלא נפדו והשמש שאכל פחות מכזית והנכרי אין מזמנין", "after": "", "opts": ["עליהם", "למקומו", "להם"], "a": 0, "ex": "אבל אכל טבל ומעשר ראשון שלא נטלה תרומתו ומעשר שני והקדש שלא נפדו והשמש שאכל פחות מכזית והנכרי אין מזמנין עליהם", "id": "b7-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b7-2", "title": "The words of zimun", "short": "Perek 7 · Mishnah 3", "parts": [2], "phrases": [["כיצד מזמנין בשלשה אומר נברך. בשלשה והוא אומר ברכו", "How does one bless in a zimun? With three, he says: \"Let us bless.\" With three and himself, he says: \"Bless.\""], ["בעשרה אומר נברך לאלקינו. בעשרה והוא אומר ברכו. אחד עשרה ואחד עשרה רבוא", "With ten he says: \"Let us bless our G-d.\" (And the same is true for) eleven and eleven myriads."], ["במאה אומר נברך לה' אלקינו. במאה והוא אומר ברכו", "With a hundred, he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d.\" With a hundred and himself he says: \"Bless.\""], ["באלף אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל. באלף והוא אומר ברכו", "With a thousand he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel.\" With a thousand and himself he says: \"Bless.\""], ["ברבוא אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו. ברבוא והוא אומר ברכו", "With ten thousand he says: \"Let us bless the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel, the G-d of hosts, the Dweller among the cherubs, for the fare that we have eaten.\" With ten thousand and himself he says: \"Bless.\""], ["כענין שהוא מברך כך עונין אחריו ברוך ה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו", "In the manner that he blesses, so the others respond: \"Blessed be the L-rd our G-d, the G-d of Israel, the G-d of hosts, the Dweller among the cherubs, for the fare that we have eaten.\""], ["ר' יוסי הגלילי אומר לפי רוב הקהל הן מברכין שנאמר במקהלות ברכו אלקים ה' ממקור ישראל", "R. Yossi says: They bless according to the numerousness of the congregation, it being written (Psalms 68:7): 'In congregations bless G-d, the L-rd from the source of Israel.'\""], ["אמר רבי עקיבא מה מצינו בבית הכנסת אחד מרובין ואחד מועטין אומר ברכו את ה'", "R. Akiva said: (We do with zimun) as we do in the house of prayer. Whether there are many or few, he says: \"Bless the L-rd.\""], ["רבי ישמעאל אומר ברכו את ה' המבורך", "R. Yishmael says: \"Bless the L-rd, who is blessed.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“himself, he says: \"Bless.” — For there is a zimun without him; and thus with all."], "mref": 2}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "How does one bless in a zimun? With three, he says: \"Let us bless.\" With three and…", "tiles": ["כיצד מזמנין", "בשלשה אומר", "נברך", "בשלשה"], "decoys": ["ברכו"], "id": "b7-2-1"}, {"t": "match", "q": "Match the number to the words", "pairs": [["שלשה", "נברך"], ["עשרה", "נברך לאלקינו"], ["מאה", "נברך לה' אלקינו"]], "he": true, "id": "b7-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 5, "to": 9, "note": ["Bartenura", "“L-rd, who is blessed.” — And the halachah is in accordance with R. Yishmael."], "mref": 2}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does R' Yishmael say?", "opts": ["ברכו את ה' המבורך", "ברכו את ה'", "נברך", "ברוך ה'"], "a": 0, "ex": "רבי ישמעאל אומר ברכו את ה' המבורך.", "id": "b7-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ברבוא אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו ברבוא והוא אומר", "after": "", "opts": ["ברכו", "תפלתו", "פטור"], "a": 0, "ex": "ברבוא אומר נברך לה' אלקינו אלקי ישראל אלקי הצבאות יושב הכרובים על המזון שאכלנו ברבוא והוא אומר ברכו", "id": "b7-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b7-3", "title": "Splitting up; two groups", "short": "Perek 7 · Mishnah 4–5", "parts": [3, 4], "phrases": [["שלשה שאכלו כאחד אינן רשאין ליחלק וכן ארבעה וכן חמשה", "If three ate together, they are not permitted to separate,. And the same applies to four or five."], ["ששה נחלקין עד עשרה ועשרה אינן נחלקין עד שיהיו עשרים", "Six may separate, until ten; but ten may not separate, until there are twenty,."], ["שתי חבורות שהיו אוכלות בבית אחד בזמן שמקצתן רואין אלו את אלו הרי אלו מצטרפים לזמון", "Two groups who ate in one house — if some of them see each other, they join for zimun;"], ["ואם לאו אלו מזמנין לעצמן ואלו מזמנין לעצמן", "and if not, each group makes a zimun itself."], ["אין מברכין על היין עד שיתן לתוכו מים דברי רבי אליעזר", "One may not make the blessing over wine until he dilutes it with water. These are the words of R. Eliezer."], ["וחכמים אומרים מברכין", "And the sages say: One does make the blessing."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“not permitted to separate” — having become subject to the obligation of zimun"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If three ate together, they are not permitted to separate,. And the same applies to four…", "tiles": ["שלשה שאכלו", "כאחד אינן", "רשאין", "ליחלק"], "decoys": ["מים"], "id": "b7-3-1"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Six who ate together may split into two groups.", "a": true, "ex": "ששה נחלקין עד עשרה.", "id": "b7-3-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 6, "note": ["Bartenura", "“makes a zimun itself” — And if one waiter serves both groups, though they do not see each other, the waiter joins them."], "mref": 4}, {"t": "mc", "q": "When do two groups in one house join for zimun?", "opts": ["When some of them can see each other", "Always", "Never", "Only on Shabbos"], "a": 0, "ex": "בזמן שמקצתן רואין אלו את אלו.", "id": "b7-3-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "שתי חבורות שהיו אוכלות בבית אחד בזמן שמקצתן רואין אלו את אלו הרי אלו מצטרפים", "after": "", "opts": ["לזמון", "אלא", "וחכמים"], "a": 0, "ex": "שתי חבורות שהיו אוכלות בבית אחד בזמן שמקצתן רואין אלו את אלו הרי אלו מצטרפים לזמון", "id": "b7-3-4"}]}];
const MB8_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "אלו דברים שבין בית שמאי ובית הלל בסעודה.", "en": "These are the differences between Beth Hillel and Beth Shammai in respect to meals.", "c": []}, {"he": "בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היום ואחר כך מברך על היין", "en": "Beth Shammai say: One blesses on the day. [First he makes the kiddush of the day] and then he blesses on the wine", "c": [["blesses on the wine", "borei p'ri hagafen. For first the day is sanctified and then the wine comes to the table because of the day. And just as the day is first in its advent, so it is first for blessing."]]}, {"he": "ובית הלל אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על היום:", "en": "And Beth Hillel say: One blesses on the wine [first] and then he blesses on the day.", "c": [["blesses on the day", "And the same holds true for one who makes kiddush over bread, for it is the wine or the bread which effect the kiddush of the day, there being no kiddush in the absence of wine or bread."]]}], [{"he": "בית שמאי אומרים נוטלין לידים ואחר כך מוזגין את הכוס", "en": "Beth Shammai say: First the hands are washed and then the wine cup is poured.", "c": [["wine cup is poured", "For if you say that first the wine cup is poured, perhaps drops will fall on the outside of the cup and become tame (ritually unclean) because of his hands. For hands, before they are washed, are of second-order tumah (uncleanliness), and they impart first-order tumah to liquids, which, in turn, render the outside of the cup tame. For liquids which have become tame impart tumah to vessels by rabbinical ordinance. They were lenient in respect to this tumah in that if the outside of a vessel became tame through unclean liquids, neither its inside, nor his hands, nor its rim become tame. And Beth Shammai hold that it is forbidden to make use of a vessel whose outside is tame even though its inside has not become tame — a decree lest drops spurt from within it to the outside of the cup and the drops become tame because of the outside and in turn impart tumah to his hands. And because it is forbidden to use a vessel whose outside is tame, first the hands are washed, and then the wine is poured, so that the drops on the outside not become tame through the hands and render the outside of the cup tame and he use the cup illicitly."]]}, {"he": "ובית הלל אומרים מוזגין את הכוס ואחר כך נוטלין לידים:", "en": "And Beth Hillel say: First the cup is poured and then the hands are washed.", "c": [["the hands are washed", "Beth Hillel hold that it is not forbidden to use a vessel whose outside is tame. Therefore, first he pours the cup and drinks it, and then he washes his hands. For if you say that he washes first and then pours the cup, it may be that the outside of the cup is tame, it being permitted to use a vessel whose outside is tame, and it may be that his hands are not thoroughly dried, so that the outside of the vessel imparts tumah to the water on his hands, and that water, having become first-order tumah, in turn makes his hands tame, and he eats with \"sullied\" hands."]]}], [{"he": "בית שמאי אומרים מקנח ידיו במפה ומניחה על השלחן", "en": "Beth Shammai say: One wipes his hands on a towel [after washing for the meal] and places it on the table.", "c": [["it on the table", "And he uses the towel throughout the meal to wipe food-grease from his hands. He may not place it on the pillow he sits on — a decree, lest the pillow be of first-order tumah and water from the drying of the hands wet the towel and, on contact with the pillow, become first-order tumah (as is always the case with liquids), and the towel, which he uses constantly in the course of the meal, impart tumah to his hands. But there is no cause for such a decree vis-à-vis a table, it being forbidden to use a table of second-order tumah."]]}, {"he": "ובית הלל אומרים על הכסת:", "en": "And Beth Hillel say: (He places it) on the pillow.", "c": [["it) on the pillow", "Beth Hillel hold that it is permitted to use a table of second-order tumah. Therefore, he may not place the towel on the table, lest the water in the towel become tame via the table and, in turn, impart tumah to the food. If he places it on the pillow, however, the only cause for concern is that tumah might be imparted to his hands — Better that his hands become tame (there being no Scriptural basis for such tumah, the Torah not requiring washing of hands for non-consecrated food) than that food become tame, there being Scriptural basis for this, first-order tumah imparting second-order tumah to non-consecrated food."]]}], [{"he": "בית שמאי אומרים מכבדין את הבית ואחר כך נוטלין לידים", "en": "Beth Shammai say: the house is swept, and then the hands are washed", "c": [["the house is swept", "The place where they ate is swept of crumbs"], ["the hands are washed", "for grace. For sometimes the waiter is an am ha'aretz and leaves over olive-size food particles; and if you say that the hands are washed first, food will be spoiled. For the waters of this latter washing will drip upon them and \"sully\" them."]]}, {"he": "ובית הלל אומרים נוטלין לידים ואחר כך מכבדין את הבית:", "en": "And Beth Hillel say: The hands are washed and then the house is swept.", "c": [["the house is swept", "Beth Hillel hold that it is forbidden to employ a waiter who is an am ha'aretz; and a waiter who is a talmid chacham (a Torah scholar) will not leave over olive-size food particles, but will remove them. And if the water drips upon particles less than the size of an olive, there is no cause for concern. For such particles may be voided to being with. The halachah in this instance is in accordance with Beth Shammai, it being permitted to employ a waiter who is an am ha'aretz."]]}], [{"he": "בית שמאי אומרים נר ומזון ובשמים והבדלה.", "en": "Beth Shammai say: (the order for blessing is:) candle, grace, spices, and havdalah.", "c": [["Beth Shammai say", "If one were eating on Sabbath afternoon and it got dark, and he had not yet finished his meal and he had enough wine for only one cup"]]}, {"he": "ובית הלל אומרים נר ובשמים ומזון והבדלה.", "en": "Beth Hillel say: candle, spices, grace and havdalah.", "c": [["spices, grace and havdalah", "All agree that havdalah is last, the departure of the (Sabbath) day being delayed, so that it not appear burdensome to him. They differ only in respect to candle and spices, Beth Shammai saying: candle, grace, and then spices; and Beth Hillel saying that candle and spices go together, for blessings that we can make, which do not give the impression of burdensomeness, such as candle and spices, we recite before grace. Beth Shammai say: \"Who created the light of the fire.\" [\"who created,\" in the past; and not \"who creates,\" which implies the future. \"the light of the fire,\" and not \"the lights of the fire,\" there being only one light in the candle."]]}, {"he": "בית שמאי אומרים שברא מאור האש ובית הלל אומרים בורא מאורי האש:", "en": "And Beth Hillel say: \"Who creates\" [the past, too, being implied] \"the lights of the fire\"", "c": [["lights of the fire", "many shades being found in the flame: red, white, and greenish."]]}], [{"he": "אין מברכין לא על הנר ולא על הבשמים של עובדי כוכבים ולא על הנר ולא על הבשמים של מתים ולא על הנר ולא על הבשמים שלפני עבודת כוכבים.", "en": "One does not make the blessing over the candle or the spices of idolators and not over the candle and the spices used for the dead, And not over the candle and not over the spices before idolatry.", "c": [["the spices of idolators", "Not over the candle, because it did not \"rest,\" the idolator having worked by its light; and it is forbidden to make a blessing over a candle that did not rest, a transgression having been committed by it. And not over the spices of idolators. The reference is to spices used in a festive gathering of idolators. And this is the intent of the latter part of the Mishnah: \"And not over the candle and not over the spices before idolatry,\" i.e., Why does one not make a blessing over the spices of idolators? For it may be assumed that a festive gathering of idolators is for idolatrous proposes and it is forbidden to make a blessing on spices used for idolatry."], ["used for the dead", "the candle (for the dead) being used for honorific purposes, and the spices being used to dispel odor."]]}, {"he": "אין מברכין על הנר עד שיאותו לאורו:", "en": "One does not bless over the candle until he benefits by it", "c": [["he benefits by it", "by its light. Not that he benefit by it, per se, but that he be close enough to benefit by it if he wishes to."]]}], [{"he": "מי שאכל ושכח ולא ברך בית שמאי אומרים יחזור למקומו ויברך ובית הלל אומרים יברך במקום שנזכר. עד אימתי הוא מברך עד כדי שיתעכל המזון שבמעיו:", "en": "If one ate and forgot to say grace, Beth Shammai say: He returns to his place and blesses; and Beth Hillel say: Until the food in his stomach is absorbed.", "c": [["his stomach is absorbed", "So long as he is not hungry because of that repast, it is a sign that the food has not yet been absorbed. And it is only in an instance of one's having forgotten, that Beth Hillel says he does not return; but, where his omission is deliberate, all agree that he returns to his place and says grace."]]}], [{"he": "בא להם יין לאחר המזון ואין שם אלא אותו הכוס. בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על המזון. ובית הלל אומרים מברך על המזון ואחר כך מברך על היין.", "en": "If wine were brought to them after the meal, and only that cup were there, Beth Shammai say: He blesses on the wine and then he says grace [for grace does not require a cup]; and Beth Hillel say: He says grace and then blesses on the wine,", "c": [["blesses on the wine", "Beth Hillel holding that grace requires a cup."]]}, {"he": "עונין אמן אחר ישראל המברך ואין עונין אמן אחר הכותי המברך עד שישמע כל הברכה:", "en": "One answers \"Amen\" after a Jew who has made a blessing; but one does not answer \"Amen\" after a Cuthite who has made a blessing unless he has heard the entire blessing", "c": [["has made a blessing", "even if he did not hear the \"Name,\" but only the end of the blessing; for it may be assumed that the blessing was \"for Heaven\""], ["heard the entire blessing", "lest he made the blessing to Mount Gerizim."]]}]];
const MB8_LESSONS=[{"id": "b8-1", "title": "Kiddush and washing", "short": "Perek 8 · Mishnah 1–2", "parts": [0, 1], "phrases": [["אלו דברים שבין בית שמאי ובית הלל בסעודה", "These are the differences between Beth Hillel and Beth Shammai in respect to meals."], ["בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היום ואחר כך מברך על היין", "Beth Shammai say: One blesses on the day. and then he blesses on the wine"], ["ובית הלל אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על היום", "And Beth Hillel say: One blesses on the wine and then he blesses on the day."], ["בית שמאי אומרים נוטלין לידים ואחר כך מוזגין את הכוס", "Beth Shammai say: First the hands are washed and then the wine cup is poured."], ["ובית הלל אומרים מוזגין את הכוס ואחר כך נוטלין לידים", "And Beth Hillel say: First the cup is poured and then the hands are washed."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“blesses on the wine” — borei p'ri hagafen. For first the day is sanctified and then the wine comes to the table because of the day. And just as the day is first in its advent, so it is first for blessing."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "These are the differences between Beth Hillel and Beth Shammai in respect to meals.", "tiles": ["אלו דברים", "שבין בית", "שמאי", "ובית"], "decoys": ["היין"], "id": "b8-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "In Kiddush, what do Beis Hillel bless first?", "opts": ["The wine, then the day", "The day, then the wine", "The bread", "Only the day"], "a": 0, "ex": "מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על היום.", "id": "b8-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“wine cup is poured” — For if you say that first the wine cup is poured, perhaps drops will fall on the outside of the cup and become tame (ritually unclean) because of his hands."], "mref": 1}, {"t": "mc", "q": "For Beis Hillel, what comes first?", "opts": ["Pouring the cup", "Washing the hands", "Sweeping", "Kiddush"], "a": 0, "ex": "מוזגין את הכוס ואחר כך נוטלין לידים.", "id": "b8-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "ובית הלל אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על", "after": "", "opts": ["היום", "המטה", "עליו"], "a": 0, "ex": "ובית הלל אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על היום", "id": "b8-1-4"}]}, {"id": "b8-2", "title": "The towel and the sweeping", "short": "Perek 8 · Mishnah 3–4", "parts": [2, 3], "phrases": [["בית שמאי אומרים מקנח ידיו במפה ומניחה על השלחן", "Beth Shammai say: One wipes his hands on a towel and places it on the table."], ["ובית הלל אומרים על הכסת", "And Beth Hillel say: (He places it) on the pillow."], ["בית שמאי אומרים מכבדין את הבית ואחר כך נוטלין לידים", "Beth Shammai say: the house is swept, and then the hands are washed"], ["ובית הלל אומרים נוטלין לידים ואחר כך מכבדין את הבית", "And Beth Hillel say: The hands are washed and then the house is swept."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“it on the table” — And he uses the towel throughout the meal to wipe food-grease from his hands. He may not place it on the pillow he sits on — a decree, lest the pillow be of first-order tumah and water from the drying of the hands wet the towel and, on…"], "mref": 2}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "Beth Shammai say: One wipes his hands on a towel and places it on the table.", "tiles": ["בית שמאי", "אומרים מקנח", "ידיו", "במפה"], "decoys": ["מכבדין"], "id": "b8-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where do Beis Hillel say to put the towel?", "opts": ["On the cushion", "On the table", "On the floor", "On the chair"], "a": 0, "ex": "ובית הלל אומרים על הכסת.", "id": "b8-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“the house is swept” — The place where they ate is swept of crumbs"], "mref": 3}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Beis Hillel say: wash hands, then sweep the house.", "a": true, "ex": "נוטלין לידים ואחר כך מכבדין את הבית.", "id": "b8-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "בית שמאי אומרים מכבדין את הבית ואחר כך נוטלין", "after": "", "opts": ["לידים", "טפלה", "מהם"], "a": 0, "ex": "בית שמאי אומרים מכבדין את הבית ואחר כך נוטלין לידים", "id": "b8-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b8-3", "title": "Havdalah", "short": "Perek 8 · Mishnah 5–6", "parts": [4, 5], "phrases": [["בית שמאי אומרים נר ומזון ובשמים והבדלה", "Beth Shammai say: (the order for blessing is:) candle, grace, spices, and havdalah."], ["ובית הלל אומרים נר ובשמים ומזון והבדלה", "Beth Hillel say: candle, spices, grace and havdalah."], ["בית שמאי אומרים שברא מאור האש ובית הלל אומרים בורא מאורי האש", "And Beth Hillel say: \"Who creates\" \"the lights of the fire\""], ["אין מברכין לא על הנר ולא על הבשמים של עובדי כוכבים ולא על הנר ולא על הבשמים של מתים ולא על הנר ולא על הבשמים שלפני עבודת כוכבים", "One does not make the blessing over the candle or the spices of idolators and not over the candle and the spices used for the dead, And not over the candle and not over the spices before idolatry."], ["אין מברכין על הנר עד שיאותו לאורו", "One does not bless over the candle until he benefits by it"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Beth Shammai say” — If one were eating on Sabbath afternoon and it got dark, and he had not yet finished his meal and he had enough wine for only one cup"], "mref": 4}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "Beth Shammai say: (the order for blessing is:) candle, grace, spices, and havdalah.", "tiles": ["בית שמאי", "אומרים נר", "ומזון", "ובשמים"], "decoys": ["בורא"], "id": "b8-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What is Beis Hillel's order when bentching falls on Motzaei Shabbos?", "opts": ["Candle, spices, bentching, havdalah", "Candle, bentching, spices, havdalah", "Bentching, candle, spices, havdalah", "Havdalah first"], "a": 0, "ex": "נר ובשמים ומזון והבדלה.", "id": "b8-3-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“the spices of idolators” — Not over the candle, because it did not \"rest,\" the idolator having worked by its light; and it is forbidden to make a blessing over a candle that did not rest, a transgression having been committed by it."], "mref": 5}, {"t": "mc", "q": "When may one say the beracha on the candle?", "opts": ["Once he can benefit from its light", "As soon as it is lit", "Only in shul", "Only on Yom Tov"], "a": 0, "ex": "עד שיאותו לאורו.", "id": "b8-3-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "בית שמאי אומרים שברא מאור האש ובית הלל אומרים בורא מאורי", "after": "", "opts": ["האש", "לפניהם", "שהוא"], "a": 0, "ex": "בית שמאי אומרים שברא מאור האש ובית הלל אומרים בורא מאורי האש", "id": "b8-3-4"}]}, {"id": "b8-4", "title": "Forgot to bentch", "short": "Perek 8 · Mishnah 7–8", "parts": [6, 7], "phrases": [["מי שאכל ושכח ולא ברך בית שמאי אומרים יחזור למקומו ויברך ובית הלל אומרים יברך במקום שנזכר. עד אימתי הוא מברך עד כדי שיתעכל המזון שבמעיו", "If one ate and forgot to say grace, Beth Shammai say: He returns to his place and blesses; and Beth Hillel say: Until the food in his stomach is absorbed."], ["בא להם יין לאחר המזון ואין שם אלא אותו הכוס. בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על המזון. ובית הלל אומרים מברך על המזון ואחר כך מברך על היין", "If wine were brought to them after the meal, and only that cup were there, Beth Shammai say: He blesses on the wine and then he says grace; and Beth Hillel say: He says grace and then blesses on the wine,"], ["עונין אמן אחר ישראל המברך ואין עונין אמן אחר הכותי המברך עד שישמע כל הברכה", "One answers \"Amen\" after a Jew who has made a blessing; but one does not answer \"Amen\" after a Cuthite who has made a blessing unless he has heard the entire blessing"]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 1, "note": ["Bartenura", "“his stomach is absorbed” — So long as he is not hungry because of that repast, it is a sign that the food has not yet been absorbed. And it is only in an instance of one's having forgotten, that Beth Hillel says he does not return;"], "mref": 6}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one ate and forgot to say grace, Beth Shammai say: He returns to his place and…", "tiles": ["מי שאכל", "ושכח ולא", "ברך", "בית"], "decoys": ["שישמע"], "id": "b8-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Until when may one still bentch?", "opts": ["Until the food is digested", "Until midnight", "Until the next meal", "Only at the table"], "a": 0, "ex": "עד כדי שיתעכל המזון שבמעיו.", "id": "b8-4-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 1, "to": 3, "note": ["Bartenura", "“blesses on the wine” — Beth Hillel holding that grace requires a cup."], "mref": 7}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Beis Hillel say one who forgot to bentch blesses where he remembered.", "a": true, "ex": "יברך במקום שנזכר.", "id": "b8-4-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "בא להם יין לאחר המזון ואין שם אלא אותו הכוס בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על המזון ובית הלל אומרים מברך על המזון ואחר כך מברך על", "after": "", "opts": ["היין", "ביום", "אומרה"], "a": 0, "ex": "בא להם יין לאחר המזון ואין שם אלא אותו הכוס בית שמאי אומרים מברך על היין ואחר כך מברך על המזון ובית הלל אומרים מברך על המזון ואחר כך מברך על היין", "id": "b8-4-4"}]}];
const MB9_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "הרואה מקום שנעשו בו ניסים לישראל אומר ברוך שעשה ניסים לאבותינו במקום הזה.", "en": "If one sees a place where miracles were performed for Israel he says: \"Blessed is He who performed miracles for our forefathers in this place.\"", "c": [["were performed for Israel", "such as the place where Israel crossed the Red Sea, the crossing of the valleys of Arnon, the crossing of the Jordan, the stone on which Moses sat when he waged war with Amalek, and the like"], ["forefathers in this place.", "Over a miracle performed for the many, such as the aforementioned, all are required to bless; but over a miracle performed for an individual, as when one sees a place where a miracle was performed for him, he must say: \"Blessed is He who performed a miracle for me in this place.\" And his son and grandson must say: \"Blessed is He who performed a miracle for my fathers in this place.\" All of the blessings of the Mishnah require mentioning of \"the Name\" and \"Kingdom,\" any blessing lacking these not being a blessing."]]}, {"he": "מקום שנעקרה ממנו עבודת כוכבים אומר ברוך שעקר עבודת כוכבים מארצנו:", "en": "(If one sees) a place from which idolatry was uprooted, he says: \"Blessed is He who uprooted idolatry from our land.\"", "c": []}], [{"he": "על הזיקין ועל הזועות ועל הברקים ועל הרעמים ועל הרוחות אומר ברוך שכחו וגבורתו מלא עולם", "en": "Over zikkim, and zevaoth [when the earth trembles and rumbles], and lightnings and re'amim, and over winds, he says: \"Blessed is He whose power and might fill the world.\"", "c": [["Over zikkim", "stars which seem to open the firmament and which dart like an arrow from place to place; or else, a star which seems to have a long tail"], ["and lightnings and re'amim", "sounds heard in the firmament from clouds pouring water into each other, viz. (Jeremiah 10:13): \"To the sound of His pouring hoards of water in the heavens\""], ["and over winds", "which blow tempestuously and which occur only occasionally"], ["might fill the world.", "And if he wishes he says: \"Blessed is He who makes the creation,\" all of these being acts of creation, viz. (Psalms 135:7): \"He made lightnings for the rain.\" But over mountains and hills, etc., he says \"Who makes the creation,\" specifically; for he cannot say: \"Whose power and might fill the world,\" these not being seen in all the world, but each in its own place."]]}, {"he": "על ההרים ועל הגבעות ועל הימים ועל הנהרות ועל המדברות אומר ברוך עושה מעשה בראשית.", "en": "Over mountains, hills, seas, rivers, and deserts, he says: \"Blessed is He who makes the creation.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ר' יהודה אומר הרואה את הים הגדול אומר ברוך שעשה את הים הגדול בזמן שרואה אותו לפרקים.", "en": "R. Yehudah says: If he sees the great ocean [Oceanus, which surrounds the world], he says: \"Blessed is He who made the great ocean\" This is so when he sees it upon occasion [after thirty days].", "c": [["made the great ocean", "it being accorded a blessing in itself because of its vastness and significance."]]}, {"he": "על הגשמים ועל הבשורות הטובות אומר ברוך הטוב והמטיב", "en": "Over rains and good reports, he says: \"Baruch hatov vehametiv\" (\"Blessed is He who is good and does good\"),", "c": [["good and does good\")", "This is so when he has land in common with another, the implication being: \"who is good (to him) and does good (to others)\"; but if he has no land at all, he says: \"We thank You, O L-rd our G-d, for every drop that You brought down for us, etc.\" And if he has land by himself, he blesses: \"shehecheyanu.\""]]}, {"he": "ועל שמועות רעות אומר ברוך דיין האמת:", "en": "and over bad tidings he says: \"Baruch dayan ha'emeth\" (\"Blessed is the true Judge\").", "c": []}], [{"he": "בנה בית חדש וקנה כלים חדשים אומר ברוך שהחיינו.", "en": "If he built a new house or bought new vessels, he says \"shehecheyanu\" (\"who kept us in life, etc.\")", "c": [["us in life, etc.\")", "Whether or not he has other vessels of the same kind, he says \"shehecheyanu.\""]]}, {"he": "מברך על הרעה מעין הטובה ועל הטובה מעין הרעה.", "en": "One blesses over an evil in which good inheres, and over a good in which an evil inheres.", "c": [["in which good inheres", "The gemara explains: as when one's fields are flooded and he loses this year's crop. Though the soil is saturated and the field made more fertile for the years to come, now, however, it is evil, and he blesses \"dayan ha'emeth\""], ["which an evil inheres", "as when one finds a lost object. Even though it is evil for him, for if the king hears of it, he will be beaten and tortured and the object taken from him, now, however, it is good, and he blesses \"hatov vehametiv\""]]}, {"he": "הצועק לשעבר הרי זו תפלת שוא כיצד היתה אשתו מעוברת ואמר יהי רצון שתלד אשתי זכר הרי זו תפלת שוא.", "en": "Crying out over what is past constitutes a vain prayer., as in one's praying: \"May it be Your will that my wife bear a son,\" when she is already pregnant;", "c": [["constitutes a vain prayer", "If one prays for what has already taken place, this is a vain prayer, for \"what has been has been\""]]}, {"he": "היה בא בדרך ושמע קול צוחה בעיר ואמר יהי רצון שלא יהיו אלו בני ביתי הרי זו תפלת שוא:", "en": "or, as in one's returning from a journey and hearing wailing within the city, praying: \"May it be Your will that it not be coming from my house.\"", "c": []}], [{"he": "הנכנס לכרך מתפלל שתים. אחת בכניסתו. ואחת ביציאתו.", "en": "One who enters a town utters two prayers, one upon entering and one upon leaving.", "c": []}, {"he": "בן עזאי אומר ארבע. שתים בכניסתו. ושתים ביציאתו. ונותן הודאה לשעבר. וצועק לעתיד לבא:", "en": "Ben Azzai says: Four, two upon entering and two upon leaving. And he gives thanks for the past and cries out for the future.", "c": [["and two upon leaving", "When he is about to enter he says: \"…that You lead me into this town in peace.\" Once he has entered, he says: \"I give You thanks for having led me into this town in peace\" — two upon entering. When he is about to leave, he says: \"…that You lead me from this town in peace.\" Once he has left, he says: \"I give You thanks for having led me from this town in peace.\""], ["out for the future", "Why all this? For one must give thanks to his Creator for the good that he has experienced and he must pray for good in the future."]]}], [{"he": "חייב אדם לברך על הרעה כשם שהוא מברך על הטובה שנאמר (דברים ו, ה) ואהבת את ה' אלקיך בכל לבבך ובכל נפשך ובכל מאדך.", "en": "One must bless the L-rd for the ill just as he does for the good., viz. (Deuteronomy 6:5: \"And you shall love the L-rd your G-d with all your heart and with all your soul, and with all your might.\"", "c": [["does for the good", "When he blesses \"dayan ha'emeth\" for the ill, he must do so with joy and with goodness of heart, just as he does when he blesses \"hatov vehametiv' for the good"]]}, {"he": "בכל לבבך בשני יצריך ביצר טוב וביצר רע.", "en": "\"with all your heart\" — with both of your inclinations, the good and the evil.\"", "c": []}, {"he": "ובכל נפשך אפילו הוא נוטל את נפשך.", "en": "\"and with all your soul\" — even if he takes your soul.", "c": []}, {"he": "ובכל מאדך בכל ממונך.", "en": "\"and with all your might\" — with all your wealth.", "c": []}, {"he": "דבר אחר בכל מאדך בכל מדה ומדה שהוא מודד לך הוי מודה לו במאד מאד.", "en": "Another interpretation: \"with all your might [meodecha]\" — For every measure (middah) that He metes out (moded) to you, [whether for good or for ill] thank Him (modeh lo) exceedingly (me'od me'od).", "c": []}, {"he": "לא יקל אדם את ראשו כנגד שער המזרח שהוא מכוון כנגד בית קדשי הקדשים.", "en": "One may not deport himself light-headedly opposite the eastern gate (of the Temple), for it is aligned with the holy of holies.", "c": [["gate (of the Temple)", "outside the Temple Mount, in the lower wall at the foot of the Temple to the east"], ["the holy of holies", "All of the gates were aligned with one another: the eastern gate, the gate of the ezrath nashim, the gate of ezrath Yisrael, the entrance of the Ullam, the sanctuary, and the holy of holies — in the days of the first Temple."]]}, {"he": "לא יכנס להר הבית במקלו ובמנעלו ובפונדתו ובאבק שעל רגליו ולא יעשנו קפנדריא ורקיקה מקל וחומר", "en": "One may not enter the Temple Mount with his staff, his shoe, his punda, and with the dust on his feet. And he should not make it kapandaria And spitting [is forbidden in the Temple Mount] a fortioti", "c": [["his shoe, his punda", "a hollow belt where money is kept. Another interpretation: a garment worn on one's flesh to absorb sweat so that it not soil his other garments. It is demeaning for one to go out in that garment alone."], ["not make it kapandaria", "to go in by that entrance and to come out by the opposite one, thereby shortening the distance. \"kapandaria\" - \"ademakifna dari, a'ol beha,\" i.e., \"Instead of circuiting rows of houses, I shall (shorten my walk and) enter here.\""], ["And spitting a fortioti", "from shoes, viz.: If the wearing of shoes, which is not a demeaning act, is forbidden there, how much more so, spitting, which is a demeaning act!"]]}, {"he": "כל חותמי ברכות שהיו במקדש היו אומרים מן העולם משקלקלו המינין ואמרו אין עולם אלא אחד. התקינו שיהו אומרים מן העולם ועד העולם.", "en": "All (prayer leaders) in the Temple would close blessings with \"from the world\" When the heretics, [who do not believe in the resurrection] distorted this, [saying: There is no world but this one], they [Ezra and his beth-din] instituted that they say: \"from the world until the world\"", "c": [["with \"from the world", "The prayer leader says at the end of every blessing: \"Blessed is the L-rd the G-d of Israel from the world until the world, the Bestower of knowledge\"; and so with all. And the answerers say: \"Blessed is the name of the glory of His kingdom forevermore.\" For \"Amen\" is not answered after every blessing in the Temple, it being written (Nechemiah 9:5): \"Arise and bless the L-rd your G-d from the world until the world,\" and, afterwards (Ibid.): \"And they shall bless the name of Your glory.\" That is, they answer: \"Blessed is the name of the glory of His kingdom forevermore.\" And we are apprised here that in the first Temple they said only: \"Blessed is the G-d of Israel from the world,\" and not more. They did not say: \"until the world.\""], ["world until the world", "i.e., there are two worlds, this world and the world to come."]]}, {"he": "והתקינו שיהא אדם שואל את שלום חברו בשם שנאמר (רות ב, ד) והנה בעז בא מבית לחם ויאמר לקוצרים ה' עמכם ויאמרו לו יברכך ה' ואומר (שופטים ו, יב) ה' עמך גבור החיל. ואומר (משלי כג, כב) אל תבוז כי זקנה אמך ואומר (תהלים קיט, קכו) עת לעשות לה' הפרו תורתך.", "en": "And they instituted that one greet his fellow in the name. For it is written (Ruth 2:4): \"And, behold, Boaz came, of Bethlehem, and he said to the harvesters: 'The L-rd be with you,' and they said to him: 'The L-rd bless you,'\" and (Judges 6:12): \"And he (the angel) said to him (Gideon): 'The L-rd be with you, O man of valor!'\" and (Proverbs 23:22): \"Do not scorn ki zakna imecha,\" and (Psalms 119:126): \"It is time to act for the L-rd; they have voided your Torah,\"", "c": [["fellow in the name", "of the L-rd, this not being regarded as denigrating the honor of the L-rd for the honor of men, \"taking\" the name of the L-rd for their sake"]]}, {"he": "ר' נתן אומר הפרו תורתך עת לעשות לה':", "en": "which R. Nathan expounded: \"They have voided your Torah at a time of acting for the L-rd.\"", "c": [["acting for the L-rd.", "If it be contended that Boaz used this blessing of his own volition and that this cannot be taken as a precedent, this is negated by the angel saying to Gideon: \"The L-rd be with you, O man of valor.\" And if it be contended that the angel is not saying this by way of greeting, but apprising him by the L-rd's embassy, that the Shechinah is with him, so that it, too, cannot serve as a precedent — this is countered by: \"Do not scorn ki zakna imecha,\" viz.: Do not scorn Boaz, saying that he acted of his own volition; but learn miziknei umathecha (\"the elders of your people\"). He has authority to reply upon, viz.: \"It is time to act for the L-rd; they have voided your Torah,\" which R. Nathan interpreted, etc., i.e.: Sometimes words of Torah are voided in order to act for the L-rd. — as in the instance of one greeting his fellow (in the name of the L-rd). This, indeed, is the will of the L-rd, viz. (Psalms 34:15): \"Seek peace and pursue it.\" It is permitted to \"void\" Torah and to do something which seems forbidden."]]}]];
const MB9_LESSONS=[{"id": "b9-1", "title": "Miracles and nature", "short": "Perek 9 · Mishnah 1–2", "parts": [0, 1], "phrases": [["הרואה מקום שנעשו בו ניסים לישראל אומר ברוך שעשה ניסים לאבותינו במקום הזה", "If one sees a place where miracles were performed for Israel he says: \"Blessed is He who performed miracles for our forefathers in this place.\""], ["מקום שנעקרה ממנו עבודת כוכבים אומר ברוך שעקר עבודת כוכבים מארצנו", "(If one sees) a place from which idolatry was uprooted, he says: \"Blessed is He who uprooted idolatry from our land.\""], ["על הזיקין ועל הזועות ועל הברקים ועל הרעמים ועל הרוחות אומר ברוך שכחו וגבורתו מלא עולם", "Over zikkim, and zevaoth, and lightnings and re'amim, and over winds, he says: \"Blessed is He whose power and might fill the world.\""], ["על ההרים ועל הגבעות ועל הימים ועל הנהרות ועל המדברות אומר ברוך עושה מעשה בראשית", "Over mountains, hills, seas, rivers, and deserts, he says: \"Blessed is He who makes the creation.\""], ["ר' יהודה אומר הרואה את הים הגדול אומר ברוך שעשה את הים הגדול בזמן שרואה אותו לפרקים", "R. Yehudah says: If he sees the great ocean, he says: \"Blessed is He who made the great ocean\" This is so when he sees it upon occasion."], ["על הגשמים ועל הבשורות הטובות אומר ברוך הטוב והמטיב", "Over rains and good reports, he says: \"Baruch hatov vehametiv\" (\"Blessed is He who is good and does good\"),"], ["ועל שמועות רעות אומר ברוך דיין האמת", "and over bad tidings he says: \"Baruch dayan ha'emeth\" (\"Blessed is the true Judge\")."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Bartenura", "“were performed for Israel” — such as the place where Israel crossed the Red Sea, the crossing of the valleys of Arnon, the crossing of the Jordan, the stone on which Moses sat when he waged war with Amalek, and the like"], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If one sees a place where miracles were performed for Israel he says: \"Blessed is He who…", "tiles": ["הרואה מקום", "שנעשו בו", "ניסים", "לישראל"], "decoys": ["דיין"], "id": "b9-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does one say on lightning and thunder?", "opts": ["שכחו וגבורתו מלא עולם", "עושה מעשה בראשית", "הטוב והמטיב", "שהחיינו"], "a": 0, "ex": "ועל הברקים ועל הרעמים... שכחו וגבורתו מלא עולם.", "id": "b9-1-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“Over zikkim” — stars which seem to open the firmament and which dart like an arrow from place to place; or else, a star which seems to have a long tail"], "mref": 1}, {"t": "match", "q": "Match each to its beracha", "pairs": [["הרים וגבעות", "עושה מעשה בראשית"], ["גשמים", "הטוב והמטיב"], ["שמועות רעות", "דיין האמת"]], "he": true, "id": "b9-1-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "על ההרים ועל הגבעות ועל הימים ועל הנהרות ועל המדברות אומר ברוך עושה מעשה", "after": "", "opts": ["בראשית", "רבי", "המזון"], "a": 0, "ex": "על ההרים ועל הגבעות ועל הימים ועל הנהרות ועל המדברות אומר ברוך עושה מעשה בראשית", "id": "b9-1-4"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 5, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“good and does good\")” — This is so when he has land in common with another, the implication being: \"who is good (to him) and does good (to others)\";"], "mref": 1}]}, {"id": "b9-2", "title": "New things, and prayers for the city", "short": "Perek 9 · Mishnah 3–4", "parts": [2, 3], "phrases": [["בנה בית חדש וקנה כלים חדשים אומר ברוך שהחיינו", "If he built a new house or bought new vessels, he says \"shehecheyanu\" (\"who kept us in life, etc.\")"], ["מברך על הרעה מעין הטובה ועל הטובה מעין הרעה", "One blesses over an evil in which good inheres, and over a good in which an evil inheres."], ["הצועק לשעבר הרי זו תפלת שוא כיצד היתה אשתו מעוברת ואמר יהי רצון שתלד אשתי זכר הרי זו תפלת שוא", "Crying out over what is past constitutes a vain prayer., as in one's praying: \"May it be Your will that my wife bear a son,\" when she is already pregnant;"], ["היה בא בדרך ושמע קול צוחה בעיר ואמר יהי רצון שלא יהיו אלו בני ביתי הרי זו תפלת שוא", "or, as in one's returning from a journey and hearing wailing within the city, praying: \"May it be Your will that it not be coming from my house.\""], ["הנכנס לכרך מתפלל שתים. אחת בכניסתו. ואחת ביציאתו", "One who enters a town utters two prayers, one upon entering and one upon leaving."], ["בן עזאי אומר ארבע. שתים בכניסתו. ושתים ביציאתו. ונותן הודאה לשעבר. וצועק לעתיד לבא", "Ben Azzai says: Four, two upon entering and two upon leaving. And he gives thanks for the past and cries out for the future."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Bartenura", "“us in life, etc.\")” — Whether or not he has other vessels of the same kind, he says \"shehecheyanu.\""], "mref": 2}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "If he built a new house or bought new vessels, he says \"shehecheyanu\" (\"who kept us in…", "tiles": ["בנה בית", "חדש וקנה", "כלים", "חדשים"], "decoys": ["לעתיד"], "id": "b9-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does one say on building a new house?", "opts": ["שהחיינו", "הטוב והמטיב", "שעשה נסים", "No beracha"], "a": 0, "ex": "בנה בית חדש... אומר ברוך שהחיינו.", "id": "b9-2-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 6, "note": ["Bartenura", "“and two upon leaving” — When he is about to enter he says: \"…that You lead me into this town in peace.\" Once he has entered, he says: \"I give You thanks for having led me into this town in peace\" — two upon entering."], "mref": 3}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What is 'crying out over the past' (הצועק לשעבר)?", "opts": ["A vain prayer", "A proper tefillah", "A beracha", "A mitzvah"], "a": 0, "ex": "הצועק לשעבר הרי זו תפלת שוא.", "id": "b9-2-3"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "היה בא בדרך ושמע קול צוחה בעיר ואמר יהי רצון שלא יהיו אלו בני ביתי הרי זו תפלת", "after": "", "opts": ["שוא", "שהוא", "ומדה"], "a": 0, "ex": "היה בא בדרך ושמע קול צוחה בעיר ואמר יהי רצון שלא יהיו אלו בני ביתי הרי זו תפלת שוא", "id": "b9-2-4"}]}, {"id": "b9-3", "title": "With all your heart", "short": "Perek 9 · Mishnah 5", "parts": [4], "phrases": [["חייב אדם לברך על הרעה כשם שהוא מברך על הטובה שנאמר ואהבת את ה' אלקיך בכל לבבך ובכל נפשך ובכל מאדך", "One must bless the L-rd for the ill just as he does for the good., viz. (Deuteronomy 6:5: \"And you shall love the L-rd your G-d with all your heart and with all your soul, and with all your might.\""], ["בכל לבבך בשני יצריך ביצר טוב וביצר רע", "\"with all your heart\" — with both of your inclinations, the good and the evil.\""], ["ובכל נפשך אפילו הוא נוטל את נפשך", "\"and with all your soul\" — even if he takes your soul."], ["ובכל מאדך בכל ממונך", "\"and with all your might\" — with all your wealth."], ["דבר אחר בכל מאדך בכל מדה ומדה שהוא מודד לך הוי מודה לו במאד מאד", "Another interpretation: \"with all your might\" — For every measure (middah) that He metes out (moded) to you, thank Him (modeh lo) exceedingly (me'od me'od)."], ["לא יקל אדם את ראשו כנגד שער המזרח שהוא מכוון כנגד בית קדשי הקדשים", "One may not deport himself light-headedly opposite the eastern gate (of the Temple), for it is aligned with the holy of holies."], ["לא יכנס להר הבית במקלו ובמנעלו ובפונדתו ובאבק שעל רגליו ולא יעשנו קפנדריא ורקיקה מקל וחומר", "One may not enter the Temple Mount with his staff, his shoe, his punda, and with the dust on his feet. And he should not make it kapandaria And spitting a fortioti"], ["כל חותמי ברכות שהיו במקדש היו אומרים מן העולם משקלקלו המינין ואמרו אין עולם אלא אחד. התקינו שיהו אומרים מן העולם ועד העולם", "All (prayer leaders) in the Temple would close blessings with \"from the world\" When the heretics, distorted this,, they instituted that they say: \"from the world until the world\""], ["והתקינו שיהא אדם שואל את שלום חברו בשם שנאמר והנה בעז בא מבית לחם ויאמר לקוצרים ה' עמכם ויאמרו לו יברכך ה' ואומר ה' עמך גבור החיל. ואומר אל תבוז כי זקנה אמך ואומר עת לעשות לה' הפרו תורתך", "And they instituted that one greet his fellow in the name. For it is written (Ruth 2:4): \"And, behold, Boaz came, of Bethlehem, and he said to the harvesters: 'The L-rd be with you,' and they said to him: 'The L-rd bless you,'\" and (Judges 6:12): \"And he (the angel) said to him (Gideon): 'The L-rd be with you, O man of valor!'\" and (Proverbs 23:22): \"Do not scorn ki zakna imecha,\" and (Psalms 119:126): \"It is time to act for the L-rd; they have voided your Torah,\""], ["ר' נתן אומר הפרו תורתך עת לעשות לה'", "which R. Nathan expounded: \"They have voided your Torah at a time of acting for the L-rd.\""]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Bartenura", "“does for the good” — When he blesses \"dayan ha'emeth\" for the ill, he must do so with joy and with goodness of heart, just as he does when he blesses \"hatov vehametiv' for the good"], "mref": 4}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the opening words", "en": "One must bless the L-rd for the ill just as he does for the good., viz. (Deuteronomy 6:5:…", "tiles": ["חייב אדם", "לברך על", "הרעה", "כשם"], "decoys": ["וחומר"], "id": "b9-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does 'בכל לבבך' mean, according to the mishnah?", "opts": ["With both your inclinations, the good and the bad", "With all your money", "Even if He takes your life", "With all your strength"], "a": 0, "ex": "בכל לבבך בשני יצריך.", "id": "b9-3-2"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 5, "to": 7, "note": ["Bartenura", "“gate (of the Temple)” — outside the Temple Mount, in the lower wall at the foot of the Temple to the east"], "mref": 4}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How did Boaz greet the harvesters?", "opts": ["ה' עמכם", "שלום עליכם", "בוקר טוב", "ברוך הבא"], "a": 0, "ex": "ויאמר לקוצרים ה' עמכם.", "id": "b9-3-3"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "One may enter Har HaBayis with his walking stick and shoes.", "a": false, "ex": "לא יכנס להר הבית במקלו ובמנעלו.", "id": "b9-3-4"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 7, "to": 10, "note": ["Bartenura", "“with \"from the world” — The prayer leader says at the end of every blessing: \"Blessed is the L-rd the G-d of Israel from the world until the world, the Bestower of knowledge\"; and so with all."], "mref": 4}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the mishnah", "before": "לא יקל אדם את ראשו כנגד שער המזרח שהוא מכוון כנגד בית קדשי", "after": "", "opts": ["הקדשים", "לבא", "רבי"], "a": 0, "ex": "לא יקל אדם את ראשו כנגד שער המזרח שהוא מכוון כנגד בית קדשי הקדשים", "id": "b9-3-5"}]}];
